k later.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nooooooo.<br /> Im guessing the abyssal book is the second choice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T08:47:17-08:00","id":1159440,"title":"","content":"*double post*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1351,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","user":"Sakii","date":". 11-16-2017, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T08:54:00-08:00","id":1159442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159431#post1159431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh, that dreaded Deathlord, The Count of Words, sending beloved tales to the unreality of Oblivion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they\u2019re a Linguistics Supernal Moonshadow Abyssal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T09:02:54-08:00","id":1159444,"title":"","content":"I have just started reading and haven't gotten very far yet. So far so good. I want some clarification about <i>Celestial Union of Blades</i> though (I searched for some keywords but couldn't find if it had been addressed already, but I admit I haven't read this entire thread). <br /> <br /> &quot;... she adds her sword-sibling's (Anima) in non-Charm bonus dice ...&quot;<br /> <br /> (Anima) = How much exactly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T09:09:55-08:00","id":1159450,"title":"","content":"Anima levels I presume. Same as you'd spend for a charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T09:14:38-08:00","id":1159452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159444#post1159444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have just started reading and haven't gotten very far yet. So far so good. I want some clarification about <i>Celestial Union of Blades</i> though (I searched for some keywords but couldn't find if it had been addressed already, but I admit I haven't read this entire thread).<br /> <br /> &quot;... she adds her sword-sibling's (Anima) in non-Charm bonus dice ...&quot;<br /> <br /> (Anima) = How much exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Equal to the current anima level. Dim=0, Glowing=1, Burning=2, Bonfire/Iconic=3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T09:21:51-08:00","id":1159455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159415#post1159415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before I move on to the Wonders chapter, a stray observation:<br /> <br /> Has anybody else noticed how the five-dot weapons in the book are all kind of evil? You've got sword that takes away memories, sword that eats people and turns them to stone, axe that eats people and turns them to sorcery, and sword to make wild, barely controlled hurricanes that tries to convince its wielder that stuff being destroyed by hurricanes is the best thing ever.<br /> <br /> When are we going to get one that seems somewhat less malevolent, I wonder. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Of Saberhagen's 12 Swords, the most boring one was Woundhealer. It was also the only one without a downside to it. Likewise, a 5 dot artifact without downsides is a little boring. Whether that is mechanical or it is story-based, it's still a downside.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T09:26:05-08:00","id":1159457,"title":"","content":"So, Wonders of the Lost Age. If this chapter is going to start with various medicines, I guess that it's a place for some assorted miscellany.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn the subject of those medicines, it's an interesting little note at the start that they only appear magical rather than being truly magic. Whatever other implications, with the change in thaumaturgy I would be glad for these things to go back to just being a matter of having the right ingredients and preparing them properly. Dawnflower seems to be the new one, and it looks like it would be fairly useful even to the Exalted. Seven bounties paste and sweet cordial are standards, but I notice that the mechanics of their effects have been technically weakened a bit here. I'm okay with that myself; as they were before, I felt that they were a bit too powerful, especially for something of their origin and nature.<br /> <br /> \u200bNow for our list of assorted items that formed part of the wonder of the First Age. I can't remember if the audient brush ever had the automatic transcription property before, but either way I think it's a good feature to have; unlimited ink is useful, but still feels a bit short of making it worth having for a player.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think clockwork birds are new, and even the lesser form of them looks quite useful (I initially misread that as a limited range of 100 miles, rather than a top speed of 100mph). Very good for maintaining communications and relationships, even before getting to the one that has more ability and initiative. It's interesting that they should have a Principle such as that; it makes me wonder at stories in which a saboteur manages to get them to stray off course by appealing to it in some way.<br /> <br /> \u200bWith the expanded capability of Lore (and its commensurate limitation), a stone containing knowledge such as that seems like a particularly valuable prize, even when it isn't solely about some kind of ancient magic. I like it. The lotus-bloom cup seems quite circumstantial, but not without use, and the Solar Seal makes me think of uses in some very political games. Thinking about it, I like the idea of it destroying the message a bit more than being unbreakable, because the former is also something that can give away how somebody unauthorised attempted to read it.<br /> <br /> \u200bLet's see, stoneheart coffer, I think that's another new one. Fairly straightforward; extremely durable lock-box. The ultimately useful tube was never exactly something that I could get behind, and I don't think its actual capabilities are any different here but... I don't know, something about the presentation gives me a stronger impression of the idea of it as a versatile tool that an enterprising Exalt could make use of.<br /> <br /> \u200bI can't say the same for the winterbreath jar, and am a little bit disappointed that it's still here. I fully acknowledge that any sense that its existence contradicts a definition for Artifacts that I came up with for myself has nothing whatsoever to do with anybody else, so that in itself is no problem, but it still strikes me as being out of place next to the rest of these items. Even the singing clockwork bird can serve as a messenger or courier, but the magical cold storage (which is the very limit of what it can do)? I don't know, maybe I should take the lack of attunement cost as an indication that this is not a thing for the Exalted.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnyway, what new and more powerful devices do they have on show...<br /> <br /> \u200bOch, Arete has an unfortunate origin story. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's a curious choice to just lay out its nature from the outset like that, but I guess for a tool other than a weapon, a bit more clarity is worthwhile. I am a bit unclear on how its first Evocation applies to different Abilities, so that might be something to clear up in a later version. Overall, I'd say it's a distinct concept for a prosthetic arm, but given the origin story and how the powers come through as Evocations, I can see how it works. It actually gives me a firmer idea for ways in which non-weapons might develop Evocations that actually maintains the concept, rather than just calling every power of an Artifact by the term.<br /> <br /> \u200bHmm, artefact armour for one's riding animal, that's very new. Not much else to say about it, but it works, and opens an interesting new possibility.<br /> <br /> \u200bI've been wary of Artifacts that only provide enhancements to dice rolls, but between the idea of it coming in the form of doubles rather than just a few extra dice, and the minor enhancement to powers a wearer might already have, I can see a more interesting method of realising that in the Dragon Tear Tiara.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Golden Hounds benefit from the novelty of Artifact running shoes, but I also find their story compelling and the mechanical realisation of their concept to be effectively intricate.<br /> <br /> \u200bI have a particular interest in magic mirrors, so I'm always looking for something to effectively realise them. For this one, I like the idea of confronting somebody with the falsehood of a Principle particularly.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Jade Steed about speaks for itself, and I unfortunately still can't quite find the Resplendent Satchel of Healing to be very interesting. The Second-Shadow Drum, on the other hand, feels like a different take on a utility Artifact with Evocations: where Arete looked like a functional prosthetic that took of a theme of self-actualisation and self-reliance due to the experience of its first wielder, and the Golden Hounds were simply something with a purpose so intimate to the maker and user that it could grow into an elaborate realisation, the Drum gives me the impression of an Artifact that was built for a specific purpose, with Evocations growing from an initially unrealised implication of that purpose. The actual powers that result being appropriately sinister helps this one to stand out.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T09:39:36-08:00","id":1159460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159416#post1159416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean... the basic fiction of a sword is to puncture someone\u2019s body until they bleed to death, so...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSo that doesn't have a number of translations, in the same book, that either don't feel the need to make the target suffer first or turn the wielder into a monster, let alone orient themselves towards a more edifying purpose?<br /> <br /> \u200bRemind me what the very first daiklaves in the book are about again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T09:49:08-08:00","id":1159464,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> I would say that the very nature of being a five dot artifact weapon requires by its very nature a being of immense power. These creatures tend to have alien concepts or desires and are so vast and powerful that it\u2019s like lashing Godzilla into a weapon (slightly hyperbolic as that is more Eva..I mean kavara). Just my two cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T10:09:28-08:00","id":1159468,"title":"","content":"Am I right to assume that the standard stat writeup should be &quot;before relevant tag modifications&quot;? If an artifact has the Balanced tag which would add +1 to Overwhelming, is it supposed to be presented as revealing the unmodified stats in the writeup and then assume that the reader adds the +1 themselves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T10:16:02-08:00","id":1159471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159468#post1159468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I right to assume that the standard stat writeup should be &quot;before relevant tag modifications&quot;? If an artifact has the Balanced tag which would add +1 to Overwhelming, is it supposed to be presented as revealing the unmodified stats in the writeup and then assume that the reader adds the +1 themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Either way, they need to specify what the standard is so we don't have to guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T10:16:05-08:00","id":1159472,"title":"","content":"It's a little inconsistent about that. The umbrella has the shield tag factored in, but the thunderbolt shield doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T10:53:55-08:00","id":1159484,"title":"","content":"Only just noticing that the table of contents is kind of weird in what it chooses the highlight... Anyway, the higher level wonders.<br /> <br /> Ohoho, look at the adorable brass Ultron. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bLooking at the Brass Legionnaires, I'd imagine that their main benefit as warriors is being enduring rather than elaborately powerful, which is still something that has its place. I feel as though a more detailed description of their capabilities in battle groups would not have been amiss, but given the parameters described in the core, it's probably not hard to figure out. Either way, I would say that is the function in which they could really shine.<br /> <br /> I wonder what certain people will make of a sidebar describing the circumstances in which Artifacts could have been made en masse? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bAhh, this is unexpected; one of those much maligned imprisonment Artifacts. I'll be interested to see what they did with that...<br /> <br /> \u200bHmm, enforcing compliance through inflicting injury, while mostly providing an out in the form of needing to kill the owner before the collar renders you unconscious. It's a bit crude (not a criticism), and certainly an improvement on the kinds of mind control in the past. Apart from its own merits, I can see some alternative concepts to build off of from this.<br /> <br /> \u200bShadow-Casting Jewel seems like it could be rather brutal under the right circumstances, seems to fit into some of my ideas about Artifacts of that level, and is a fun combination of soulsteel darkness control and moonsilver witchery. That the sorcery-catching cord is limited to one spell makes me think of stories in which one needs to be very discerning and meticulously plan what spell they wish to be able to call on at a moment's notice, which I regard as fitting to the character archetype.<br /> <br /> \u200bHmm, I think in prior Editions, Wings of the Raptor were much more literal, so I approve of changing the concept to give room to something more like myth or folklore. Errrm... oh, I initially misread the line as saying that you needed to be Resonant to unlock the basic flight power, rather than it needing to be purchased by the Dissonant (who then get an inferior version), that makes more sense. This would be a case in which I think of Evocations less as a matter of unlocking new powers, and more as a representation of growing mastery over the basic power.<br /> <br /> Now, for the first product of outright First Age Artifice. I'm pretty sure that the Golden Serpent was in prior Editions, but if I ever read anything about it I can't remember. Rather than a comparison, I'll just judge this write-up in its own right, and say that if I had any doubt about its lofty position, that was alleviated when I got to the line about how it can absorb knowledge from everybody that it kills. The image of somebody going around with a pet golden snake draping their shoulders or slithering alongside them, to be sent sneaking into places as an assassin and reconnoitre is rather vivid. I'm also amused by the notion that the metal snake is something with some very powerfully held convictions.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Veil that Holds Back Time certainly has a rather powerful effect, although one that I would suspect has its greatest use in things that players encounter, rather than their own activities.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd finally, some rules for siege engines. That these things use War and require the assistance of a battle group is already a good start to making me feel like the concept is well-integrated into the combat system, and I'd say that the resulting damage stats make them feel appropriately powerful if they manage to hit somebody (even if it probably takes a few shots to build up the Initiative for a good decisive attack, even if the result is likely extreme). I definitely think that it was a good call to streamline all of the engine varieties into a number of broad categories; too many kinds of catapult before.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo, lightning ballista and implosion bow; these are things that I've been wondering about for a while. Looking at the descriptions, their base forms definitely look like they're the kinds of things that simply cannot be operated with the Exalted or similar people (even if they're commanding a team rather than doing all of the heavy lifting personally). Still, that really only affects a personal image of what the First Age was like (which can be resolved in a few ways besides), and it is fitting to their place in the Age of Sorrows (even accounting for other possible folks who could attune, command and power their Evocations on behalf of some mortal prince), so it isn't really a problem.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe lightning ballista's Stormblast Barrage does seem fairly powerful, and the statement that it requires repair after every use is certainly a lot more succinct than prior Editions with their &quot;after X shots the thing becomes 10% less effective, whatever the hell that means&quot;, but if it can only be used for attacks on people with the Evocation, and the Evocation can only get off one shot at a time... No, wait, I just misread the last paragraph, it requires repair <u>after a scene</u> in which the Evocation is used. So it can still be shot multiple times, for withering and then decisive attacks (albeit with heavy mote costs), and then when the fight is concluded it requires repair. Makes perfect sense.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhereas the implosion bow... Collapsing Point of Destruction does look as though it could be fairly dangerous, but it raises the question of how the shooter is meant to build up Initiative for the decisive attack before firing, unless I'm missing something in the numbers and it would be the kind of thing that could be dangerous just on the Initiative of one's Join Battle roll (or else that it's something where you're in the thick of the battle until the point where you leap over to command your implosion bow crew and have them open fire). Also, I think the language describing how people's dodges interact with it is a bit unclear, and not phrased through the usual combat mechanics, so that could do with some cleaning up.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd finally some vehicles. I think it's a good touch to give Horizon Endeavour a bit of personal backstory, and it looks as though it would be quite fast. I've wondered how naval artillery would work since the core established a standard damage, so building around that by inflicting disadvantages looks like a decent way to go. The Chariot of Aerial Conquest is fast, but looks a bit bare-bones (even if I imagine that such flight would have particular tactical and strategic advantages in the context of the game, both in terms of nobody to effectively contest aerial superiority, and conveying the Exalted around).<br /> <br /> \u200bNow, while I do like hearthstones as a general thing, in a book such as this they have difficulty fighting for my attention. So while I am interested in reading these ones, and maybe even commenting upon them, for the time being I'm going to leave them aside. I'm eager to get a look at the warstrider chapter, so I'll get right to that in a little while.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T10:58:11-08:00","id":1159486,"title":"","content":"The collar is basically Sun Wukong's headband, so I guess it can pass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T11:06:29-08:00","id":1159487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159464#post1159464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> I would say that the very nature of being a five dot artifact weapon requires by its very nature a being of immense power. These creatures tend to have alien concepts or desires and are so vast and powerful that it\u2019s like lashing Godzilla into a weapon (slightly hyperbolic as that is more Eva..I mean kavara). Just my two cents.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bApart from not being part of the guidelines or parameters given for Artifacts of such power, and how an Artifact such as Volcano Cutter has neither an entity bound into it or any kind of mystery that could be used to suppose that maybe it does, that's <i>supremely</i> limiting as a way to approach five-dot Artifact weapons compared to the diverse array of concepts before them.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat, orichalcum weapons never get to express their concepts of majesty, righteousness and revelation at the highest level? All of those concepts peak at four-dots, and then it's straight into being a monster's prison?<br /> <br /> \u200bI want to be clear, I didn't mean that point before as a criticism, more of a wry observation. It just seems extremely weird for people to run with that observation and come up with arguments for why it should represent an indelible standard. Especially considering some of the really great concepts that the writers seeded throughout the preceding Artifacts; my God, there's an axe that lets you weaponize insight into the world and the people you're fighting against, made from the discarded brush of an art god, and I've got people (on two forums, mind) telling me that of course five-dot Artifacts are going to be sinister and malevolent because you stick people with the pointy end? Come on.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd to be absolutely clear, this is not a crack against the writers. I think all four of those weapons are great, and considering everything that came before, I don't doubt that they have the imagination and creativity to come up with five-dots that would touch on a more diverse array of sensibilities.<br /> <br /> Just perplexed by responses saying that those things don't belong and are unnecessary.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T11:11:58-08:00","id":1159490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159487#post1159487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bApart from not being part of the guidelines or parameters given for Artifacts of such power, and how an Artifact such as Volcano Cutter has neither an entity bound into it or any kind of mystery that could be used to suppose that maybe it does, that's <i>supremely</i> limiting as a way to approach five-dot Artifact weapons compared to the diverse array of concepts before them.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat, orichalcum weapons never get to express their concepts of majesty, righteousness and revelation at the highest level? All of those concepts peak at four-dots, and then it's straight into being a monster's prison?<br /> <br /> \u200bI want to be clear, I didn't mean that point before as a criticism, more of a wry observation. It just seems extremely weird for people to run with that observation and come up with arguments for why it should represent an indelible standard. Especially considering some of the really great concepts that the writers seeded throughout the preceding Artifacts; my God, there's an axe that lets you weaponize insight into the world and the people you're fighting against, made from the discarded brush of an art god, and I've got people (on two forums, mind) telling me that of course five-dot Artifacts are going to be sinister and malevolent because you stick people with the pointy end? Come on.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd to be absolutely clear, this is not a crack against the writers. I think all four of those weapons are great, and considering everything that came before, I don't doubt that they have the imagination and creativity to come up with five-dots that would touch on a more diverse array of sensibilities.<br /> <br /> Just perplexed by responses saying that those things don't belong and are unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>And now I am <i>really</i> looking forward to your review of Kavara...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T11:22:19-08:00","id":1159492,"title":"","content":"The Forgotten Blade doesn't seem to have a spirit or anything in it. <br /> <br /> So yeah, I think people are seeing a pattern where there isn't one. Having powerful artifacts have a drawback like that is an easy way to make plot, but it's by no means the only one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T11:26:07-08:00","id":1159494,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Before getting to warstriders, one thing that I feel confident of at this point is that Holden's statement about how the book would provide more context and meaning to those terms such as century and thousand-year daiklaves seems to have not made it through. Whether this was a result of limited space or a change in ideas along with developers, I could not say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T11:28:41-08:00","id":1159497,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">https://www.</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">youtube.com/watch?v=FckkZihQUaU<br /> <br /> The Average exalted who pilots Kavara</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T11:36:00-08:00","id":1159504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159492#post1159492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having powerful artifacts have a drawback like that is an easy way to make plot, but it's by no means the only one.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bEhhh, I wouldn't really think of it in terms of drawbacks...<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm looking at Volcano Cutter and... I can't remember its name, the boomerang, as contrasts. Volcano Cutter might have a bit of an issue with where you use it, but that's not really anything to do with its personality, just that its powers are about creating eruptions. I see the basic matter of its high-level power being the way in which it needs to build up and deposit its energies through use in combat, and can only pull off its major effect by harnessing those. A matter of requiring momentum.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe boomerang is similar in terms of its capabilities and ultimate power, and while there are people who might have reservations about it using souls, its character and the focus of its abilities isstill on pursuing criminals.<br /> <br /> Really, setting aside any sinister implications, the biggest thing that I take from the Forgotten Blade is just being an alternate approach to a weapon of significant power, in the way that its lowest attuned state can still do a very powerful thing, with Evocations to refine the application. I think you could make a red jade reaper daiklave that has a similar approach to some kind of heat based effect, without needing to be about desiccating everything within a large radius.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T11:40:27-08:00","id":1159508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159494#post1159494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmmm...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Before getting to warstriders, one thing that I feel confident of at this point is that Holden's statement about how the book would provide more context and meaning to those terms such as century and thousand-year daiklaves seems to have not made it through. Whether this was a result of limited space or a change in ideas along with developers, I could not say.</div> </div> </div> </div>I almost feel like they dropped that aspect. Or at least sorta. <br /> <br /> Now it seem like you get to be a 4-dot or 5-dot daiklaive based more on how epic and evocative your themes are. Perhaps it's more an idea that you only see a daiklaive such as this forged every thousand years type thing? Though that doesn't make sense in the context of the first age either where these were churned out much faster than in the current age. *shrugs* maybe now it's just plain hyperbole?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T12:30:36-08:00","id":1159517,"title":"","content":"Look at the descriptions of the artifacts listed, and count how many have existed for centuries/millennia/uncounted years. I think that's the difference. These artifacts that have been around for a while and used here and there are well developed like the examples we have. Fresh artifacts, as the book notes, will only have 1-2 Evocations and are waiting for a wielder to turn them into a legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T12:41:09-08:00","id":1159519,"title":"","content":"Also, for the people doing Reads... When you get to the Warstrider section, I recommend this background music.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9EEtGLLDhNY\" data-code=\"9EEtGLLDhNY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/9EEtGLLDhNY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T13:53:10-08:00","id":1159550,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oIscL-Bjsq4\" target=\"_blank\">Until they get to Karvara, of course.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T15:22:48-08:00","id":1159592,"title":"","content":"All right, the big one: warstriders.<br /> <br /> The opening is standard; establishing what warstriders are and how they're used (with the addition of a bit of terminology for them based on their Artifact level); laying out the fact that they have Evocations (covering both a broad array of powers and representation of things like ancillary systems); the image of how they're piloted, and implications therein (particularly how actions and abilities between pilot and warstrider being equivalent, excepting things like the warstrider's Strength and soak).<br /> <br /> Now, the idea that warstrider Strength is linked to pilot Strength, and they run on a different track to determine feats of Strength, I think is the first new thing. If nothing else, it would feel like a good instance of making that image that piloting them entails being strapped into a harness and pulling the limbs around feel real and visceral. I also think it's a good idea to just say, in this case, that they can perform certain feats irrespective of their general Strength rating is a good way to let them have both heavy lifting and breaking without being wholly broken when it comes to hitting you with a sword.<br /> <br /> Let's see, soak, Hardness and health levels sell the idea of them being hardy. I'm surprised that there's still a difference between mundane and Artifact weapons for warstriders. Still, if the traits are all the same as the regular scaled one, the odd character who would be able to wield them wouldn't be immensely broken (depending a bit on what their Evocations are like).<br /> <br /> Trying to figure out the devastating action... so if the warstrider is engaged with enemies that include a battle group (or a lot of trivial opponents, which I assume is contextual depending on whether or not you're in a warstrider; as in, there might be certain enemies who weren't trivial until you strapped into a 10m suit of god armour), you get to make an attack against them without it needing to use up whatever attack you'd want to make against a more dangerous specific enemy. I'm guessing this is something that came out of playtesting; an observation at some point that the scope and power of a 'strider didn't come across as well if they needed to make a choice between attacking armies and Exalts. It also gives another sense of why one might employ such a weapon, since a regular-sized Exalt can still be a bit vulnerable to the stronger battle groups, especially if they're less focused on hitting back because their attention is focused on Exalted or similar enemies.<br /> <br /> There's an interesting balance in mobility; at combat scale, their enormous size means they can move around and make or close distance with ease, but are comparatively slow and hulking when it comes to moving across long distances. They get all of the benefits of Legendary Size (plus some that are unique, that I'm going to read as a matter of being not only large, but having a human stance and physical awareness), and their huge combat advantages are offset a bit by the difficulty of moving with enough precision to effectively strike singular, human sized enemies. I personally appreciate the direct statement that the things are so heavy that it can present major environmental difficulties to them, if only for how this plays into certain old stories about defeating the things.<br /> <br /> I'd say that the rules for maintenance and repair of the things are appropriately onerous, without being impenetrable to read, and actually make the prospect of the thing taking damage seems like something rather fearsome. That going especially for cases where a play group simply won't have a character with the skills necessary to repair one; I have this nice mental picture of a group travelling with their warstrider in tow, and every major battle carries a lot of tension around the question of just how banged up it's going to get and how much further they can go before it needs to be abandoned altogether, or they have to seek out some dubious power that will perform the repairs for a price. I can readily imagine that as the origin for any ruined warstrider frames that a character might try to jury rig back into a state of functionality.<br /> <br /> Then there are the anti-warstrider gambits. I've sung the praises of gambits before, especially as they pertain to adding a bit of diversity and verisimilitude to circumstances such as these, and even while the gambit for simply creating an opening to just attack the pilot is appropriately difficult, it does overall give me an impression that taking a warstrider into battle against a reasonably powerful human is not necessarily the best course of action. They're definitely powerful, but not in a way that forces an arms race.<br /> <br /> Still, a lot of that is old news, even when it's expressing it through a new system. I'm about ready to look at the examples of specific warstriders and see what they can really do now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T16:43:41-08:00","id":1159619,"title":"","content":"How I feel when Glorious Solar Saber can be applied to Warstriders<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/uvnY2HopaQA?t=97\" data-code=\"uvnY2HopaQA\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/uvnY2HopaQA/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> How I feel when reading Karvara, and then remembering that Glorious Solar Plate and Glorious Solar Saber can be applied to Warstriders<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HdapxblHV5k?t=210\" data-code=\"HdapxblHV5k\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/HdapxblHV5k/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21242-charonferryman","name":"CharonFerryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T16:52:59-08:00","id":1159621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159125#post1159125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read ahead for the Striders. The Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation made my Archery-favoring Lookshy Twilight squee and clap like a six-year-old girl who just got a pony for Christmas</div> </div> </div> </div>Its the Gundam Heavy Arms Custom!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21242-charonferryman","name":"CharonFerryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T17:31:38-08:00","id":1159632,"title":"","content":"I just realized something-<br /> <br /> If they are still a thing (and if they are not a thing, I will make them a thing), the main thing Hellstriders have over Warstriders is that they're <i>cheap.</i><br /> <br /> Well, not cheap, but much less dependent on technical knowledge and infrastructure to make-they're all actually giant demons in fused armor suits. To make them, all you need is a bunch of demons to merge into one and enough material to armor the giant mess of eldritch muscle. That doesn't mean it's easy, but you don't need a cabal of sorcerers, an expert in several fields, and an understanding of First Age Artifice to make one, and demons have a lot more infrastructure for Artifact construction to begin with.<br /> <br /> Of course, the main problem with driving a Hellstrider is, in fact, it's a giant demon-all Hellstriders have minds of their own, and if they don't like a pilot, they won't let themselves be attuned. The binding isn't nearly as strong as it is with Karvara, and if you don't make the Hellstrider happy, it's entirely possible for it to realize it is a giant robot and your friends are not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T17:54:29-08:00","id":1159642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159632#post1159632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just realized something-<br /> <br /> If they are still a thing (and if they are not a thing, I will make them a thing), the main thing Hellstriders have over Warstriders is that they're <i>cheap.</i><br /> <br /> Well, not cheap, but much less dependent on technical knowledge and infrastructure to make-they're all actually giant demons in fused armor suits. To make them, all you need is a bunch of demons to merge into one and enough material to armor the giant mess of eldritch muscle. That doesn't mean it's easy, but you don't need a cabal of sorcerers, an expert in several fields, and an understanding of First Age Artifice to make one, and demons have a lot more infrastructure for Artifact construction to begin with.<br /> <br /> Of course, the main problem with driving a Hellstrider is, in fact, it's a giant demon-all Hellstriders have minds of their own, and if they don't like a pilot, they won't let themselves be attuned. The binding isn't nearly as strong as it is with Karvara, and if you don't make the Hellstrider happy, it's entirely possible for it to realize it is a giant robot and your friends are not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is in the Q&amp;A but Hellstriders got rolled in with Warstriders. You can see this pretty clearly with Kavara that the same space can be filled with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T17:55:55-08:00","id":1159643,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the Juggernaut is a Warstrider with Evocations...<br /> <br /> edit: Vance says it's not","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-16-2017, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T18:04:52-08:00","id":1159648,"title":"","content":"Does anyone else think it's kind of weird that in the hearthstone section abyssal hearthstones immediately jump to greater?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T18:34:44-08:00","id":1159658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159648#post1159648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone else think it's kind of weird that in the hearthstone section abyssal hearthstones immediately jump to greater?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really. It makes sense that they're rare enough in Creation that only the super-important ones are worth showing at this point - and more comparatively common ones will be introduced with the Abyssals and the Underworld as a setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T19:23:06-08:00","id":1159671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159648#post1159648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone else think it's kind of weird that in the hearthstone section abyssal hearthstones immediately jump to greater?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not any weirder than all Lunar Hearthstones being standard. Or there being one less Abyssal stone than Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T19:24:12-08:00","id":1159672,"title":"","content":"All-Conquering Colossus: The story of this one strikes me as being the archetypal warstrider, even with the slight twist of the love story motivating its creation and how that informs its resulting powers. I do actually derive amusement from the idea that the thing was inadvertently presented as a romantic gift in the form of being able to effectively fight off being impulsively attacked by the object of affection; where's <i>that</i> in our Marvel movies, eh? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As for the powers themselves, they mostly reflect that story; it's your basic concept of a warstrider, the big armour to fight opponents that are very large, very strong, or both, in various elaborations of strength and durability (with hints of that underlying purpose in the occasions where proven durability enhances strength). While I imagine that later warstriders will have a bit more flash to them, I actually like at least one of them to have that sense of focus, while still proving the concept of expressing their power in Evocations. Hell, assuming that none of the others date to the War, I could even use all of that to add a bit of flavour in my own mind with the notion that part of the simplicity derives from it being one of the earlier examples. All in all, I'd say that this was a good one to start off with.<br /> <br /> Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation: It's nice to see the Scorpion Empire make a return, as well as a warstrider focused on ranged combat. If All-Conquering Colossus was a straightforward one for brawling, this one is similar in terms of laying down a barrage of firepower. I find it to work, though, partially because of the addition of various diagnostic tools, and because the contrast between how the Artifact siege weapons function here and how they did when standing alone gives a certain sense of power and purpose beyond it just being a warstrider with an implosion bow welded on. It helps that it has things such as Reality-Stabilizing Cannonade to maintain a certain mystical flavour for it. And the description of Godsigh of Noonday Triumph makes me want to play Asura's Wrath again (or find a new game of a similar style to try out) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> Crusading Spear of the Depths: Was Oadenol always a Sidereal? Eh, doesn't matter. So, warstrider specialized for submarine combat. It doesn't specify so, but I assume that Crusading Spear is buoyant enough to effectively swim and remain suspended if its pilot wishes. While I do like the preceding warstriders, it is nice to see one whose capabilities are a bit more diverse, making good use of its concept. In just this one, you've got improved underwater mobility and senses, a cascade to create a signature attack, various forms of defensive water manipulation.<br /> Emerald Chevalier: Huh, a centaur-esque warstrider. It's a bit odd, but I suppose it's a good idea to showcase something to give a sense of diverse possibilities for them. What's most interesting here is this concept of using a warstrider as a means of taking a particular fighting style and then scaling it up.<br /> <br /> Godspeed Vanguard: One of those more stealth-oriented warstriders that they brought up in the outline. This would be another one I can find less to say about, although I find its realisation of overcoming a natural limitation of the warstrider to be effective, and do like the afterimage based Evocation.<br /> <br /> Now, for the royals.<br /> <br /> Ascendant Nova Phoenix: Hmm, unusually massive <i>and</i> capable of flying. I'll be interested to see how its Evocations realise those feats attributed to it. Looking over it, it definitely does feel powerful, although depending how far into the Evocation cascade a character has taken it, possibly something that requires the chronicle to have taken a very extreme direction to feel as though it's getting its full use (or to keep it from being simply overwhelming). A high mobility transportation Charm feels like a curious choice for the pinnacle, but... I guess anything more would be redundant compared to the preceding arsenal, and this ultimate power gives a sense of omnipresence to it; a notion that at the height of its power, no matter where a threat might arise, this devastating response would be able to arrive either in time to stop the threat or avenge its victims. Between this and the other orichalcum warstriders, while I wouldn't model the powers of the Unconquered Sun off of him, it does give me this image in which he was a typical source of inspiration behind their construction.<br /> <br /> Karvara, the Walking Devil Tower: Hmmm... hmmm... oho.<br /> <br /> \u200bY'all built it up too much; it's okay.<br /> <br /> So that's all of the warstriders. I'd say that they've done a fairly good job of elevating the concept, and realising its initial promise. I'll summarise my overall thoughts on Arms of the Chosen at a later time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T19:30:15-08:00","id":1159674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159672#post1159672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Karvara, the Walking Devil Tower: Hmmm... hmmm... oho.<br /> <br /> \u200bY'all built it up too much; it's okay.<br /> <br /> So that's all of the warstriders. I'd say that they've done a fairly good job of elevating the concept, and realising its initial promise. I'll summarise my overall thoughts on Arms of the Chosen at a later time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit that I was hoping for a more detailed reaction to Kavara if for no other reason that it has a really interesting story to it. Although it might just be me, no idea why I am so intrigued by the story of the 101.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T21:50:54-08:00","id":1159719,"title":"","content":"I just caught that Sozen is a The Usual Suspects reference. That's hilarious. <br /> <br /> Overall, this book is fantastic. It's already made me rethink everything I thought I knew about evocations. I'm really excited to bring this to the table. At this point, Arms has got me pondering and salivating and gluttonous for the next books to become available!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10995-abakus","name":"Abakus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T00:12:08-08:00","id":1159739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159674#post1159674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit that I was hoping for a more detailed reaction to Kavara if for no other reason that it has a really interesting story to it. Although it might just be me, no idea why I am so intrigued by the story of the 101.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAhh, that's no fun. Call my bluff why don't you...<br /> <br /> Very well, here's what I actually wrote about it:<br /> <br /> Karvara, the Walking Devil Tower: The origin story of this one is neatly detailed; if nothing else, it should satisfy people who were dissatisfied by prior Editions never letting Lunars accomplish anything cool without dying. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I also like the turn of phrase saying that being unable to exist in Creation meant that if it was somewhere, Creation would be the thing to go. As for its mechanics... it's funny to see that this is the only warstrider that can be attuned only by a certain kind of Exalt. Assuming that they don't have Limit Tracks, even Ascendant Nova Phoenix could be wielded by a Terrestrial, but Karvara cannot because they would be insufficiently corruptible. On that note, this really is a fearsome extension of prior examples of corrupting Artifacts, fitting to its elevated state both as a warstrider and N/A level. Consider its Evocation development, I guess that a necessary narrative path for one to take while associated with this warstrider is to seek out scenarios that provoke Limit, which can probably be expressed in-character in a number of ways. It's also interesting to consider how some of Karvara's effects, such as aiding in social influence or more-or-less erasing people from existence, might create an impulse to use it in situations unusual for a warstrider; more low scale and personal. I could really see that playing into a narrative of the warstrider getting under a pilot's skin, luring them into donning it with greater frequency and at times when the force would seem unnecessary; I have this picture of the uncanny scenario of one's circlemates realising that one is starting to wear it almost all the time, or some petitioner coming for an important meeting with an Exalt and being disturbed to find them conducting business from inside this distinctly terrifying machine.<br /> <br /> \u200b(I later commented on the notion that Karvara might spend a lot of its time getting to know you and discerning your Intimacies, so that when it assumes control one of its highest priorities is to go around systematically eating and erasing people whom you care about, until one day its pilot wakes up under the impression that the warstrider is the only meaningful relationship that they've ever had.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T07:15:22-08:00","id":1159828,"title":"","content":"Here's my short reactions to each of the weapons, along with a personal grade:<br /> <br /> 3-Dot Weapons<br /> <br /> <b>Courange and Galliard:</b><br /> I love these artifacts. While its fairly restrictive in that you need two characters to use them, it is a perfect example of intermingling story and mechanics. The capstone - fusing into a single being - is flavorful, but I feel likely to be clunky. 5/5<br /> <br /> <b>The Distaff:</b><br /> Not as much of a fan here. The story is also fantastic, and it has a great arc presented through story and mechanics, but the other charms are lacking. This is largely due to interacting extensively with grapple and crafting rules, both of which are weak. 2/5 purely on the strength of the story<br /> <br /> <b>The Fist of Titans:</b><br /> Story isn't nearly as interesting as the first two, but it provides a neat mechanical minigame via generating and using charges. Unfortunately, charges are very limited, and can only be generated with Aim actions, so it is difficult to use the other evocations. Despite this, it shows good unity of themes and solid mechanical weight. 3/5<br /> <br /> <b>Frost-Thorn Knuckles:</b><br /> Another pretty dull story, but great mechanical execution. Its just really really good at killing things, with a secondary focus on surviving the cold. This is a really niche focus though, and makes them less useful anywhere outside of the North - and likely the far north. 3/5<br /> <br /> <b>Hawk Star's Jess:</b><br /> Really boring. It's a sling, which doesn't evoke much awesomeness, and it's just literally David vs Goliath. It introduces a promising Doom mechanic, and then never uses it in interesting ways. I cannot imagine making a character that actually uses this, just because it's so dull. 2/5<br /> <br /> <b>Heartsong:</b><br /> Story is okay. Not as dull as the previous few, but not really gripping either. But I love these evocations. It uses the under-used Custom Gambit concept, and then builds on it and ties in some other lesser-used aspects of social interaction as well. It's missing a really great capstone to bring it together though. 4/5<br /> <br /> <b>Heaven and Earth Gauntlets:</b><br /> Pretty interesting story, and a plausible reason for a player to have them. Evocations are also pretty good, working with Smash attacks, but also not really great. Capstone needs a few more examples too. 3/5<br /> <br /> <b>Irenio's Bell:</b><br /> Interesting story, and a great fluff description. Its defensive, and most of its powers are reactive rather than proactive, but still seem fun to use. I worry that its ability to break non-artifacts and summon second circle demons is too powerful for a simple evocation, but you get them at later Essence levels anyway. 3.5/5<br /> <br /> <b>Rainwalker:</b><br /> It's an artifact umbrella shield, with a decent origin story. Combine that with good evocations and ties in to Water's concepts of flow and redirection, and I really like the result. 4/5<br /> <br /> <b>Razor Dancer and Wise Steel:</b><br /> Gah. It's a fantastic concept for evocations - basically rooting a new martial art within the weapons - but its wasted on a &quot;new&quot; artifact as an excuse to not write up more evocations. Hugely disappointing in the end, I want to see more of this. 2/5<br /> <br /> <b>Summer Thunder:</b><br /> Pretty weak story, but an interesting combination of effects for evocations. Horse archery is cool, but relatively unexplored. I like its growth from a simple skirmishing weapon to a true war-leader's symbol later on. The lack of truly unique effects holds it back somewhat. 3.5/5<br /> <br /> <b>Sun's Brush:</b><br /> Another fantastic concept, a weaponized brush. It ties combat and lore together nicely, and has a full suite of cool evocations. Nothing really jumps out at me as character-defining, but its all useful and fun. 4/5<br /> <br /> <b>Tusk of Galaech-Ma:</b><br /> Boring story, interesting mechanics. It's about what you'd expect from &quot;spear used to hunt things&quot;, but it's solid overall. 3/5<br /> <br /> 4-Dot Weapons<br /> <br /> <b>Asphodel:</b><br /> A really great concept and story behind the first intelligent artifact in the book. Its evocations are fine, if a bit plain, but they serve the story well. The biggest drawback is the storyteller complexity tied to the bargains and retainers 4/5<br /> <br /> <b>Burning Branch:</b><br /> Another cool story, and a great variety of evocations. Its combination of fire and green jade make for some unique abilities, but I don't like its heavy use of Disarm, which is a gambit that makes combats less interesting. 3.5/5<br /> <br /> <b>Flying Silver Dream:</b><br /> A cool artifact, and one that may fight better than your character. It adds complexity to combat by having essentially a second character to control, and its capstone is essentially undefeatable except by ST fiat. I love the concept, but I doubt I would want it in my game. 3/5<br /> <br /> <b>Gnomon:</b><br /> Another great artifact, it combines an interesting story with an evocation tree that really lives up to the idea that 4-dot artifacts create their own style of fighting. Its time-twisting powers couple well with its larceny support, and the capstone is a unique story addition. 4/5<br /> <br /> <b>Mistweaver:</b><br /> Also fantastic. Its story provides a usable seed for an adventure, and it creates a unique opportunity for stealth combat. I like the way it uses the mists to enhance using stealth in combat while also providing ways to counter it so that it doesn't become one sided. A great artifact 4/5<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmare Shard:</b><br /> This one's just alright. It's got a cool concept, but its heavy focus on fighting the wyld makes it very niche. Also, its infection angle doesn't seem very useful, as it slowly drives victims mad over the course of days. 3/5<br /> <br /> <b>Sekhem:</b><br /> Love the concept and most of the Heat system. I really don't like the random chance to basically lose the artifact until downtime though, and would definitely house rule in an alternate penalty for Cracking. Other than that, it's really solid and a great fire weapon. 3.5/5<br /> <br /> <b>Shipbreaker:</b><br /> It breaks ships. That's about it, which is disappointing for a 4-dot artifact. You don't want to invest this much into a weapon that only works against huge enemies, because outside of specific campaigns that's not going to come up very often. 2.5/5<br /> <br /> <b>Sirrush:</b><br /> Starts off so cool, and then crashes down. It's an air-aspected flamepiece that doesn't fall into the idea of shooting lightning, and it gets some cool abilities with that combination. But then it starts using Ammunition Checks as a mechanic, which approximately 0 people have ever used. Terrible idea to base half an evocation tree around 2/5<br /> <br /> <b>Strife's Crucible:</b><br /> An amazing story, concept and fighting style. This feels more like an NPC artifact than a PC one, but leads to interesting stories either way so I like it. 4/5<br /> <br /> <b>Sunflash:</b><br /> An incredible artifact. Its themes remain strong throughout, and it provides great story hooks in the form of Kiragaru. Unfortunately, it doesn't really describe the god, which isn't good given that the gods appearance and personality are part of the evocations. 4/5<br /> <br /> <b>Talion:</b><br /> Another really good artifact. It's got a great story potential, and fits a common character archetype. Its evocations and story mesh nicely together, but the evocations feel a little lacking overall. 4/5<br /> <br /> <b>Vainglory:</b><br /> A well done social/combat artifact, it ties its themes together very well. I like the Conceit system, although it could do with a couple more evocations hanging off of it to modify the value. While the final tree is a bit lacking, it still feels solid with great themes. 4/5<br /> <br /> <b>Zelator:</b><br /> Incredible weapon, I just wish we knew more about the Hexmanse. It's also exactly what you would wish for in an anti-sorcerer weapon, being able to both fight directly and lead armies. Being a weapon used against sorcerers and also buffing sorcery feels a bit weird though. 4.5/5<br /> <br /> 5-Dot Weapons<br /> <br /> <b>The Forgotten Blade:</b><br /> I'm not a big fan of the concept of this weapon, but I recognize that other people are, and this is a very well done execution of the idea. 4/5<br /> <br /> <b>Gorgon:</b><br /> Awesome imagery, it's a great example of a demon weapon done right. I wish it did something with the people turned to stone, but it's an army killer 5-dot. 4.5/5<br /> <br /> <b>Soulfarer:</b><br /> Well, this is the artifact for people who want to do combat sorcery. It's a pretty classic soul-drinker weapon combined with sorcery stuff that feels like it may be OP but I'm not sure. I'd have preferred it if it stuck more with just the soul-drinking rather than working sorcery in, but it's a great artifact either way. 4/5<br /> <br /> <b>Stormcaller:</b><br /> A really cool storms artifact, similar to a concept I did in a previous game. Intensity works because it provides multiple paths to improvement and ties in to most of the evocations. I do worry that it will lead to some bad blood among players, since it leads to friendly fire. And did we really need 3 &quot;evil bound demon weapons&quot; in the 5-dots? 4.5/5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/776-saintedphysician","name":"SaintedPhysician","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T09:54:56-08:00","id":1159894,"title":"","content":"So, my last word on the book:<br /> <br /> \u200bMagic items, especially weapons, are always a hard sell to me. Even on their own, I think they often have difficulty expressing a capability that really makes them feel worthwhile or lively, and in a game system they have a difficult balancing act between effectively conveying those powers and being balanced mechanically. That gets even more complicated when they're part of a setting in which other forms of magic exist; the distinction between what a device can do and a person (or whatever other forms of magic) can always seem fuzzy, and they often feel redundant against one another.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe basic concept of Evocations felt from the beginning like a very good way to navigate this, and the core book felt like it had good potential, but with room for development; not enough examples to paint a full picture, but still a firm foundation.<br /> <br /> \u200bThis book has really brought them home. It's more than them just feeling legitimately powerful, realising the potential of Evocations to give an Artifact powers that are nuanced and expansive, without being all over the place, and either meaningfully different from what their wielders can do on their own or having a sense of alignment with them. It's the way that the Artifacts really feel alive, dripping with personality, history, <i>purpose</i>, and they help bring the setting to life along with them. And there's enough variety here to not only intrigue in their own right, but provoke the imagination for what other Artifacts could be; I've always believed in the credo of them all being unique, but this provides a clearly grasped foundation to actually realise that.<br /> <br /> And to have extended this as far as warstriders is a real achievement.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's more than just something that made magical weapons feel real and meaningful to me; it's a book that excites me to the same degree that Masters of Jade did, and I can think of no higher praise than that.<br /> <br /> \u200bTo the developers and writers, I say well done, and thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T10:02:31-08:00","id":1159902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaintedPhysician</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159828#post1159828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Sirrush:</b><br /> Starts off so cool, and then crashes down. It's an air-aspected flamepiece that doesn't fall into the idea of shooting lightning, and it gets some cool abilities with that combination. But then it starts using Ammunition Checks as a mechanic, which approximately 0 people have ever used. Terrible idea to base half an evocation tree around 2/5</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1085191-ammunition-check-survey\">They had a thread about this.</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T10:48:55-08:00","id":1159919,"title":"","content":"So I'm loving the hearthstones. I'm a little disappointed to not fine concussive essence cannons either under siege weapons or regular weapons but there's enough between the two books to piece together how they should work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T11:58:59-08:00","id":1159945,"title":"","content":"Honestly I think essence cannons are redundant under the 3e paradigm. I mean, &quot;essence goes in, hurt comes out&quot;? We got you covered brah. It's called Sekhem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T12:10:16-08:00","id":1159952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159013#post1159013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea, I think, is that specifics can be defined by the ST while broad strokes give you an idea.<br /> <br /> What I absolutely love is that it's like a giant apology letter for WotLA. Four weapons, one armor, and a frickin' WARSTRIDER, forged by Sidereals -- where WotLA forgot that Sidereals could actually craft. And Oadenol reveal aaaaaaa. A giant apology in the form of a backflip with two middle fingers firmly raised.</div> </div> </div> </div>The odd thing is that Oadenol was always a sid of serenity, I have no idea why that was in the Treaties of Black and White (pg.35) and not Oadonel's actual codex...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T12:43:50-08:00","id":1159976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159494#post1159494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmmm...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Before getting to warstriders, one thing that I feel confident of at this point is that Holden's statement about how the book would provide more context and meaning to those terms such as century and thousand-year daiklaves seems to have not made it through. Whether this was a result of limited space or a change in ideas along with developers, I could not say.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always assumed it was the same way they talked about 100 Year and 1000 Year Floods.<br /> <br /> &quot;A sword like that only comes along once in a thousand years...&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/100-year_flood\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Kaskaskia_Island_1993_flooding.jpg/1280px-Kaskaskia_Island_1993_flooding.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/100-year_flood\" target=\"_blank\"> 100-year flood - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/100-year_flood\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/100-year_flood </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T12:51:40-08:00","id":1159978,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if that's how it was originally intended - but that's the best explanation for how to interpret it with how canon has shaken out. I read it as &quot;daiklaives this powerful are a century/millennium long project to forge&quot; originally, but obviously that doesn't work with either the crafting rules, or the narratives we have (though, if a Solar did dedicate a millennium to forging a specific Artifact, that would be a good central hook to that specific Artifact's narrative of it's great power [along with what ever motivated a Solar to do that]).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-17-2017, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T13:01:04-08:00","id":1159983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159902#post1159902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1085191-ammunition-check-survey\">They had a thread about this.</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am completely shocked that anyone would actually do this. Well, my personal rating stands because Ammunition coming up at all in Exalted is dumb","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/776-saintedphysician","name":"SaintedPhysician","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T13:19:09-08:00","id":1159991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159976#post1159976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always assumed it was the same way they talked about 100 Year and 1000 Year Floods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe I suggested something to that effect in response to somebody in a different forum, to which Holden brought in that it was something a bit more concrete that they intended to detail a bit in Arms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaintedPhysician</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159983#post1159983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I am completely shocked that anyone would actually do this. Well, my personal rating stands because Ammunition coming up at all in Exalted is dumb</div> </div> </div> </div>Way to double down, there. {eye-rolling smiley}<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T19:42:48-08:00","id":1160092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaintedPhysician</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159983#post1159983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I am completely shocked that anyone would actually do this. Well, my personal rating stands because Ammunition coming up at all in Exalted is dumb</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh, I think it's fine in Exalted. I've seen plenty of wuxia/kug-fu movies that had ridiculous amounts of ammo for a fighter only to eventually pull at &quot;Oh fuck, this is my last one! Gotta make it count!&quot;<br /> Much like in Feng Shui, the &quot;Run out of ammo when dramatic/cool&quot; is perfectly at home in Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T20:25:45-08:00","id":1160101,"title":"","content":"This is a good book. I liked every artifact. Every goddamn one. The two dot ones are my favorites, strangely enough, but all the ones with evocations are appropriately legendary. None of them were run of the mill, each was unique. <br /> <br /> Which is a damn sight better than in 2nd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T21:51:09-08:00","id":1160121,"title":"","content":"In in loregasms! Niobraran War! Zen-Mu! Interloping devil stars! My beloved Scorpion Empire! Evocative (heh) timeline names! So much goodness.<br /> <br /> I particularly liked the fiction in this book. There's not one I didn't like.<br /> <br /> Great art! The art for Crusading Spear of the Depths in particular ravishes me.<br /> <br /> Good job, all artists, writers, and developers! I'm even more excited for Dragon-Blooded and The Realm!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/740-anaximander","name":"Anaximander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T05:57:03-08:00","id":1160183,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure it's the right place to post this (sorry if it's not)<br /> <br /> Anyway : it's a great PDF book with a bunch of errata being stockpiled. Does anyone know when/if the errata-ed PDF book will come ? Or if the hard version will be errata-ed ?<br /> <br /> (BTW I think it's a very good idea to let the fanbase errata the book ^.^ )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>French Exalt &amp; ST &amp; ToolMaker [<a href=\"http://refhi.free.fr/\" target=\"_blank\">Website</a>]<br /> Advanced Character Generator <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1087290-advanced-character-generator#post1087290\" target=\"_blank\">Thread, </a><a href=\"http://refhi.free.fr/exalted3/Fiche%20perso%20colab.xlsx\" target=\"_blank\">Excel Version</a> &amp; <a href=\"http://refhi.free.fr/exalted3/Fiche%20perso%20colab.ods\" target=\"_blank\">LibreOffice Version</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141199-exalted-3-familiar-generator\" target=\"_blank\">Familiar Generator Thread</a> &amp; <a href=\"http://refhi.free.fr/exalted3/Familiar%20Generator.ods\" target=\"_blank\">Libreoffice Version</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13355-refhi","name":"Refhi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13355_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T06:25:26-08:00","id":1160188,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the printed version has errata. That's why you can't get it printed yet. Usually takes about a month or two, when CofD books have done the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T07:18:04-08:00","id":1160200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159519#post1159519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, for the people doing Reads... When you get to the Warstrider section, I recommend this background music.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9EEtGLLDhNY\" data-code=\"9EEtGLLDhNY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/9EEtGLLDhNY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/S1VFqsew26c\" target=\"_blank\">I raise you.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T07:48:40-08:00","id":1160212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1160200#post1160200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/S1VFqsew26c\" target=\"_blank\">I raise you.</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As much as I adore Pacific Rim, sorry Kyman201, I'm on Gallus' side.<br /> <br /> And I don't care if a description says otherwise somewhere, this is how Warstrider's are piloted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YK38WzlNvfk\" data-code=\"YK38WzlNvfk\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/YK38WzlNvfk/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"http