ey":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T14:33:59-08:00","id":1160307,"title":"","content":"Is there a weapon/armor that enhances a commander ability to lead an army?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11395,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11395-shaddar","user":"Shaddar","date":". 11-18-2017, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11395-shaddar","name":"Shaddar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"338"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T14:44:45-08:00","id":1160312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159415#post1159415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anybody else noticed how the five-dot weapons in the book are all kind of evil?</div> </div> </div> </div>It reinforces an implicit theme of the game: power corrupts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11690-mizzlfoshizzl","name":"mizzlfoshizzl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T15:23:24-08:00","id":1160329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mizzlfoshizzl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1160312#post1160312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It reinforces an implicit theme of the game: power corrupts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about that, it seems more like just a groove writers were in to me.<br /> The other high tier artifacts aren't all sorts of nastiness. Five-dot armour isn't evil, the five-dot siege weapon isn't evil, nor are the five-dot+ warstriders all evil (and the later can do mass destruction).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T15:24:54-08:00","id":1160332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shaddar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1160307#post1160307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a weapon/armor that enhances a commander ability to lead an army?</div> </div> </div> </div>Zelator and Summer Thunder have those themes off the top of my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T15:26:35-08:00","id":1160334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shaddar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1160307#post1160307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a weapon/armor that enhances a commander ability to lead an army?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well what else do you want with it? Like being able to visit &quot;the forge&quot; is a solid power, but do you want it to be able to retrieve items from it like a handy haversack, do you want it to be able to absorb raw materials like Asphodel? <br /> <br /> Cause a suggestion to my mind would be a modified version of Asphodel with a smith god, or demon in it that can help create weapons, armor, and what have you, or just a being capable of passing out the item you request.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T15:28:59-08:00","id":1160336,"title":"","content":"I want to know if Artifacts like these &quot;Shields&quot; would be Noble Warstriders, or something lesser for which there is no longer an official classification.<br /> <br /> (5:28, 5:48)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/OYPF-GwuVIc?t=324\" data-code=\"OYPF-GwuVIc\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/OYPF-GwuVIc/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Perhaps a middle point between powered armors and Warstriders? Too big to be one, not big enough to be the other.<br /> <br /> <i>RWBY's</i> Paladin mecha is a similar size class.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ljpDvGhT-_M\" data-code=\"ljpDvGhT-_M\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ljpDvGhT-_M/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-18-2017, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T15:39:20-08:00","id":1160341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1160334#post1160334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well what else do you want with it? Like being able to visit &quot;the forge&quot; is a solid power, but do you want it to be able to retrieve items from it like a handy haversack, do you want it to be able to absorb raw materials like Asphodel?<br /> <br /> Cause a suggestion to my mind would be a modified version of Asphodel with a smith god, or demon in it that can help create weapons, armor, and what have you, or just a being capable of passing out the item you request.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be like a hand sized mobile workshop, i can set it up, and store or retrieve materials and tools. Puting my hand on a pile of jade, and absorb it would be a nice trick but it wouldnt be a main thing. <br /> <br /> <br /> Btw, I messed up the threads and post than question here instead of the Ask the Devs, thats why the question is different now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11395-shaddar","name":"Shaddar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"338"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T16:05:33-08:00","id":1160346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Major</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1160329#post1160329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure about that, it seems more like just a groove writers were in to me.<br /> The other high tier artifacts aren't all sorts of nastiness. Five-dot armour isn't evil, the five-dot siege weapon isn't evil, nor are the five-dot+ warstriders all evil (and the later can do mass destruction).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think its simply we're confusing the cause and the result. It isn't &quot;Evil is the result of power&quot;, its more &quot;it takes a massive amount of work to seal away a demon inside a sword.&quot; Which means Sealing a Demon Inside a Sword *needs* to be Artifact 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T16:07:31-08:00","id":1160348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mizzlfoshizzl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1160312#post1160312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It reinforces an implicit theme of the game: power corrupts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just... just read some more of my posts after that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T16:52:47-08:00","id":1160362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1160348#post1160348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just... just read some more of my posts after that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did, and while I agree with you that it needn\u2019t be an \u201cindelible standard,\u201d I stand by the assertion, especially in light of 3rd edition\u2019s explicit Moorcock influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11690-mizzlfoshizzl","name":"mizzlfoshizzl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T17:43:17-08:00","id":1160373,"title":"","content":"It's funny, I wrote all of that before I even got to the 5-dot giant suit of armour that is made of love (and it's stronger than you).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T18:02:07-08:00","id":1160381,"title":"","content":"I think it's notable that the most Evil!!! armor is 4 dot (Sozen or Five Edicts).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T19:38:14-08:00","id":1160393,"title":"","content":"My own first read through review.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*I dislike <b>having </b>to create homebrew (I prefer to have a guided system* I can throw away if I want), so I imagine some folks may be at odds with the following perspective.</span><br /> <br /> The sample artifacts are for the most part quite good. Ditto for the chapter fiction in helping create a life to the artifacts.<br /> <br /> I had an expectation that the book would have more in-depth explanation of artifact/evocation creation than it does. After reading the design section I do not feel any more capable of creating artifacts/evocations compared to what the core offered.<br /> <br /> Artifacts having added additional complexity is something I find interesting and engaging (time period, resonance, etc.). However, the lack of concrete explanation on how to scale powers up or down for these newly added bits of complexity leaves creation to feel entirely like guesswork to me; the page and three-quarters devoted on how to build stuff (pp.18-19) left me desiring much more hand-holding. The end result for me is copy &amp; pasting from existing artifacts without much of an idea of how their powers are fair for the level of evocation and artifact.<br /> I was hoping for something like a point-buy system* similar to the 2E manse system, or other systems (like DND, PFRPG) item creation systems to expedite the process that could be used in addition to the free-form system.<br /> <br /> As abstract charm and artifact building seems to be the way forward for EX3 (I am praying point-buy comes back for manses) I find myself wanting a different artifact &amp; evocation build system. Anyone know of any fan-made systems for doing such?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T20:43:43-08:00","id":1160403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159259#post1159259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God, I love First Age Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so<br /> Get a Solar or DB. Have them unlock the Evocations from Fist of Titans.<br /> Get a Solar and have them unlock the Evocations of the Heaven and Earth Gauntlets.<br /> Get a very sturdy Demon or Raksha.<br /> Have the two exalts stand a range band apart and use Smashing attacks to knock the enemy back and forth<br /> Congratulations, you've just invented Creature of Darkness Ping Pong!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T00:57:41-08:00","id":1160446,"title":"","content":"Is anyone else planning on using the Key to the Dream Palace for training time? Obviously it can't be used for physical attributes, but that won't stop my Dawn from leveraging a perfect opportunity to demonstrate techniques in a setting where her students can't actually get hurt. Paradise is a dojo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T09:38:22-08:00","id":1160536,"title":"","content":"I had a notion about five-dot Artifact weapons in which the thing in common between them isn't so much a power that corrupts, as a power that is great enough to require being handled with care.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhen thinking about their basic comparisons measured against the lower levels, the term that came to my mind is that five-dots are <b>brimming</b> with power. That can come in forms such as the corebook, where they accumulate and unleash energy just from being used in combat, or some of our new ones with things like an entry-level power that is quite strong, up to things like Stormcaller where just pulling the thing out causes a growing manifestation; all depending on the Artifact's temperament. You're holding a lightning bolt, something that twists around and vibrates in your hand, and while it's not necessarily dangerous to you, you've got to keep a tight grasp to actually direct it.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's how I would characterize the cascade of their Evocations; three-dots' flow into you, adding some colour to the edges of your actions, and four-dots' try to shape you, creating a channel for you to act within, while five-dots have their own thing going on and your part is to focus and refine that, bending the manifestations of its power to your own will and needs, whether that be applying that in ways that are somewhat novel, or at least pointing it in the direction you want before taking the latch off the door. Depending on its nature, that might sometimes make you open to some kind of influence, but it's mostly a subject of keeping a handle on this power as you use it (since, in most cases, the Artifact can hardly use itself).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T12:47:30-08:00","id":1160608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1160536#post1160536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(since, in most cases, the Artifact can hardly use itself).</div> </div> </div> </div>Even that four dot animated Moonsilver sword needs to be activated.<br /> <br /> Edit: Moonlit Silver Dream, I think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 11-19-2017, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T13:33:11-08:00","id":1160633,"title":"","content":"Well I've been waiting a long time for this book<br /> <br /> But I will say this; it's good stuff. Great work. Looks better than the core too! Very nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T14:29:32-08:00","id":1160652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ketrus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1160446#post1160446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is anyone else planning on using the Key to the Dream Palace for training time? Obviously it can't be used for physical attributes, but that won't stop my Dawn from leveraging a perfect opportunity to demonstrate techniques in a setting where her students can't actually get hurt. Paradise is a dojo.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the fact that it's a great way to enjoy some comfort when you have to travel light and rough it in the wilderness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T19:09:46-08:00","id":1160731,"title":"","content":"Also, a thing I adore about Arms.<br /> <br /> I never once had a moment of &quot;So what does THAT mean?&quot; or &quot;Wait, what's this Evocation even do?&quot;<br /> <br /> There are some artifacts where my reaction was a bit lukewarm, but I never once questioned what something DID. Really speaks well to the hopeful clarity of the Dragonblood book","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 11-19-2017, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T21:22:54-08:00","id":1160762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1160227#post1160227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean this?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://78.media.tumblr.com/69a5af1dfd909b131473ff92351870be/tumblr_ozmhziqFVc1sateyko1_400.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Yeah, those don't look like leather straps to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I did in fact mean that, and while I get why it was done that way (More dramatic in a still image, I guess?) I hate it with a burning passion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T09:49:20-08:00","id":1160892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1160731#post1160731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a thing I adore about Arms.<br /> <br /> I never once had a moment of &amp;quot;So what does THAT mean?&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;Wait, what's this Evocation even do?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> There are some artifacts where my reaction was a bit lukewarm, but I never once questioned what something DID. Really speaks well to the hopeful clarity of the Dragonblood book</div> </div> </div> </div>100% this. Clarity is playability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T10:18:39-08:00","id":1160900,"title":"","content":"Speaking of clarity, I really appreciated the reminder in the Warstrider section that they are created with Craft: First Age Artifice. While there was a side-bar earlier the reminder in the section was very helpful as it saves people from hunting.<br /> This seemed particularly important to me as craft from the core often leaves players wondering which craft is relevant to what project with what stretch of the imagination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T11:17:31-08:00","id":1160918,"title":"","content":"Going back few years, to how the previous developers likened previous treatments of the different character types in the game to &quot;building heat&quot; in wrestling. I appreciated how in the intro for the warstrider chapter, neither the Dragon Blooded nor Volfer came across as a chump. The dragonblooded was cool headed and competent while Volfer was a terrifying creature ready to rip apart a warstrider all by himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T12:30:21-08:00","id":1160939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1160918#post1160918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going back few years, to how the previous developers likened previous treatments of the different character types in the game to &amp;quot;building heat&amp;quot; in wrestling. I appreciated how in the intro for the warstrider chapter, neither the Dragon Blooded nor Volfer came across as a chump. The dragonblooded was cool headed and competent while Volfer was a terrifying creature ready to rip apart a warstrider all by himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got to say, this is important for me not just for playability for each Exalt, but it also really helps player perception of other Exalts. If a Solar player in a Solar only campaign sees every dragonblooded character in fiction as only a chump to be eliminated for the glory of their solar magnificence, they're going to develop certain mentalities in play.<br /> <br /> If Dragonblooded are at least depicted as underdogs who in the right moment can slay even the greatest, it'll give that player some pause in thought when the ST says &quot;this campaign will be set in a realm controlled region&quot; even if its just &quot;how many resistance charms should I invest in to not die&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T14:56:20-08:00","id":1160974,"title":"","content":"Does anyone else feel that Karvara's first two Evocations, Eat the Heart of God and Berserker Fury Blitz, are a little underwhelming? The former is basically free, so it's nice to have, but I doubt the few points of initiative it gives would make much of a difference in most situations. The latter seems like it's rarely worth the cost unless you absolutely, positively have to pull off some feat of strength, or you're in Limit Break and using it to enhance a decisive attack.<br /> <br /> Karvara is awesome, don't get me wrong. But that's why it was the first thing I looked at when I opened the book, and when I saw those two Evocations as the first example of what warstriders can do... I felt a bit disappointed in them until I read the rest of the chapter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/157-phoenix_kensai","name":"Phoenix_Kensai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar157_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T15:09:08-08:00","id":1160979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phoenix_Kensai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1160974#post1160974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone else feel that Karvara's first two Evocations, Eat the Heart of God and Berserker Fury Blitz, are a little underwhelming? The former is basically free, so it's nice to have, but I doubt the few points of initiative it gives would make much of a difference in most situations. The latter seems like it's rarely worth the cost unless you absolutely, positively have to pull off some feat of strength, or you're in Limit Break and using it to enhance a decisive attack.<br /> <br /> Karvara is awesome, don't get me wrong. But that's why it was the first thing I looked at when I opened the book, and when I saw those two Evocations as the first example of what warstriders can do... I felt a bit disappointed in them until I read the rest of the chapter</div> </div> </div> </div>On it's own, Eat the Heart of God is decent. But remember that you don't have to pay anything to get it, you get it for free when you attune to it, so it's functionally a baseline power of the artifact. From there, many of the other Evocations build off of it and do amazing effects using EtHoG as your trigger. This is the core of the design. A basic free power that you'd use all the time because it's easy, but later on you get big benefits from using it in unique situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T16:50:42-08:00","id":1161004,"title":"","content":"Eat the Heart of God is a set up for God-Monster Apotheosis, which is a massive Evangelion reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T18:42:46-08:00","id":1161034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1159519#post1159519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, for the people doing Reads... When you get to the Warstrider section, I recommend this background music.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9EEtGLLDhNY\" data-code=\"9EEtGLLDhNY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/9EEtGLLDhNY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>So I guess Karvara will use<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4JziGeqPamM\" data-code=\"4JziGeqPamM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/4JziGeqPamM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum