d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T09:23:46-08:00","id":1161894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1161882#post1161882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, I'm only ironically annoyed. I know how fandoms work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Call it the Island of the Frozen Ma(i)ze.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T09:37:15-08:00","id":1161897,"title":"","content":"Something I just noticed, which I didn't notice before because of how well it worked.<br /> <br /> To whomever is responsible for separating out the evocations with a different background colour than the hearthstone base powers, I love you!<br /> I found this makes it way easier to read the powers &amp; ability section without things bleeding into one another.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T10:45:26-08:00","id":1161913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1161882#post1161882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, I'm only ironically annoyed. I know how fandoms work.</div> </div> </div> </div>No! You can't let us know your frustrations are ironic! Now half the fun of calling it Frosty Dorito Island is gone!<br /> <br /> (I'm joking)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T16:09:25-08:00","id":1161991,"title":"","content":"Arms of the Chosen inspired in me an idea for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1149666-heart-s-blood-predation-and-limited-theft-symbiosis-and-unlimited-sharing?p=1161038#post1161038\">a moonsilver ring that would let Lunar Exalted use the Heart's Blood of living victims against them in a way that would be utterly broken if it were done through Lunar Charms.</a><br /> <br /> It amuses me that my other idea, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1161047-combine-the-might-of-a-warstrider-with-the-lunar-power-of-heart-s-blood\">a Warstrider that borrows Lunar's Heart-Blood for shapeshifting into behemoths</a>, represents the complete opposite side of the scale. One tiny artifact and one huge artifact.<br /> <br /> A perfect Changing Moon and Full Moon pair of artifacts, really.<br /> <br /> The No Moon artifact would be one that takes advantage of moonsilver's sorcerous potentials; a sorcerous phylactery geared for spells that transform targets.<br /> <br /> I don't know what physical shape this artifact would take, but I like the idea of a Lunar using it to countermagic a spell to turn someone into an animal, and then using the stolen motes and an Evocation to turn around and curse the other sorceror into an animal's shape. Or to use the motes to fuel her own Heart's Blood transformations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T12:55:47-08:00","id":1162241,"title":"","content":"If I ever get a chance to play another Supernal Thrown character (I probably won't, they're silly), I'll take the Frost-Thorn Knuckles on them. They're fantastically mean, and I eagerly anticipate the look on the Storyteller's face when he or she realizes that wound penalties, Joint-Wounding Attack, and Glacial Beast Claw has reduced an antagonist's Dexterity + Dodge pool to zero.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I'm not sure what to make of Ravening Fimbulwinter Approach. It's a neat charm, but it treats the results of a rush roll as a reflexive attack in a way that seems to be unprecedented. Here's an example, as I understand it. The wielder of the Frost-Thorn Knuckles rushes an enemy and rolls seven successes to their three successes. They activate Ravening Fimbulwinter Approach, and attack (unrolled) with the four remaining successes. If this exceeds or matches the defender's Defense, they roll the relevant decisive damage dice.<br /> <br /> The ambiguity comes from adjudication of the defender's charm use. When does the defending character declare parry or evasion enhancers? Do they have to declare charms like Dipping Swallow Defense or Dodge Excellency during the initial rush, or can they spend essence after the rush is successful? If it's the latter, they receive the benefit of being able to spend precisely enough essence to avoid the attack. If it's the former, they're forced to spend essence defending against an attack that might never happen. What's the correct play here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T14:25:45-08:00","id":1162259,"title":"","content":"Does anyone else refer to the benefits you get to first attuning to an Artifact it's &quot;attunement bonus&quot;?<br /> <br /> Because they all still have one, even if it's just unlocking the first Evocation. I think it's better to have a name for this precedent than not, so why not reuse a term from previous Editions?<br /> <br /> <br /> As to Warstriders, how many of you think that the player's Gundam to the enemy's Zaku is best represented by giving the player a Royal (NA) Warstrider whereas the enemy has a Noble (5-dot) Warstrider?<br /> <br /> For a game where the enemy has plenty of Zakus to send against your Gundam, would you want them to be something weaker and more easily produced than a Noble Warstrider?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T14:29:02-08:00","id":1162260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1161639#post1161639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to see trauma bear snuck into many books as we go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you think he's been through enough?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T22:19:24-08:00","id":1162362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1162259#post1162259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to Warstriders, how many of you think that the player's Gundam to the enemy's Zaku is best represented by giving the player a Royal (NA) Warstrider whereas the enemy has a Noble (5-dot) Warstrider?<br /> <br /> For a game where the enemy has plenty of Zakus to send against your Gundam, would you want them to be something weaker and more easily produced than a Noble Warstrider?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't help but think that this mindset is exactly the opposite of what the Devs were trying to do with Warstriders. Each Warstrider is a weapon and a legend in its own right. A single Strider deployed against an army should make the army collectively shit itself.<br /> <br /> If 'plenty of Zakus' are deployed, that kind of missed the point of Warstriders. Even Noble Striders include things like the All-Conquering Colossus, or the Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation.<br /> <br /> Edit: If you want your Striding PC to go up against similarly sized opponents, you can probably have a Realm Warstrider using the basic stats mentioned with no Evocations for an opponent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 11-25-2017, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T22:42:38-08:00","id":1162364,"title":"","content":"It is definitely not the interest of Exalted 3e by default to have minion warstriders.<br /> <br /> If you want to put them in, I\u2019d just make them without evocations. It\u2019s... kind of bland, but hey, if you want minion striders, that\u2019s kind of the result of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T01:11:00-08:00","id":1162382,"title":"","content":"I'd probably say that if you want to use Ex3's Warstrider rules for that sort of thing then go for it, but I wouldn't use the setting, because the setting in no way supports minion Warstriders. Like you're looking at a battle with one on each side being crazy rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T04:02:19-08:00","id":1162424,"title":"","content":"The setting has in the past supported 'minion' warstriders, and can do it again just fine. To produce minion warstriders you do it the same way you do minion everything else, stick it in a battlegroup. Battlegroup are super flexible like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T05:35:27-08:00","id":1162441,"title":"","content":"I'd suggest using Golems or relatively simple (non-First Age Artifice) Automata of appropriate size, instead of creating &quot;Mookstriders&quot;. Brass Legionnaires can apparently be created in batches with appropriate infrastructure, so it might be feasible for larger automata as well, by using even more resources and support structure. The minions being computer-piloted is a thing occasionally in Gundam, right?<br /> <br /> If you feel you must have some sort of lesser Warstriders instead of other options, however, Make them Artifact 4-5 Non-First Age Artifice things that can be produced in batches like Brass Legionnaires, don't give them Evocations, and possibly make them attunable by mortals at the cost of much of their life, Gunzosha style.<br /> I'd say these should be less powerful than even the basic Warstrider Chassis - say a baseline of Soak 13, reduce Health levels by one or two of each type, Strength caps at 5 or 6 (and up to about 10 or 12 for Feats of Strength), give them no mobility bonus, or even a penalty for heavier models, remove the ability to use Devastating actions, or restrict it in some way (using it gives you onslaught-like penalty, or costs Willpower, or consumes your movement action, or can only be used once per scene - possibly with a reset condition, or whatever other cost or restriction you deem appropriate). Possibly ease up on some of the weaknesses if the thing is attuned to an Essence User<br /> <br /> Observe that, even considering non-FAA automata or lesser Warstriders, even the Realm could not field Gundam-like numbers of them as mooks in the standard setting of the Age of Sorrows. If you want a gundam-like game you are gonna have to adjust the setting accordingly.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T09:18:47-08:00","id":1162734,"title":"","content":"Finally bought the book today. How come Exalted can't seem to get decent art? It's got less totally appaling pieces than the core, but the quality of the art overall is not what I would expect from a professionally done book.<br /> <br /> A shame, since in all other regards, my first impression is that this is a very, very good book. Minton and Vance seem to know their stuff indeed.<br /> But dear lord, why pay artists who understand neither perspective, nor anatomy? I know there's people in the world who can draw faces, why have none of them been hired?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T09:27:40-08:00","id":1162739,"title":"","content":"Now that we've got more examples of it, there's an implication of Artifact temperament and legend that I would be interested in running with, regarding differences in their power across the Ages.<br /> <br /> \u200bPreviously, I always found something a bit tricky about differences of power between First and Second Age; it felt to me as though the First Age should have had things that were in some way superior to the products of the Second (particularly the latter half) without it solely being a matter of Artifact level. It could get a bit of that out of the sense of &quot;there were ways to make this thing in abundance, where now it takes a dedicated crafter months at least&quot;, but that wouldn't work for everything (especially the likes of daiklaves). Similarly, it's not a difference that Craft (Magitech) was well-suited to resolving, and particularly not when Craft (First Age Artifice) defines itself primarily by things that would significantly alter the setting aesthetic; a daiklave in principle won't do that, but it feels as though there should be daiklaves that they made in the First Age that you wouldn't really find later on.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo, as an example, Beloved Adorei; a daiklave that Arms specifically called out as actually alive and intelligent. On top of that, some of its Evocations are distinctly powerful, even if they come with some appropriate conditions. Yet, it remains a 3-dot daiklave. Is this the kind of thing that could be readily made through much of the Age of Sorrows?<br /> <br /> \u200bLeaving aside the question of whether anybody would have the facility for crafting orichalcum besides the Solars; the subject of how magical material resonance plays into crafting hasn't really been brought up, because the craft system is a lot more abstract than that, so I would assume for the time being that just about anybody can make an Artifact from anything (also leaving aside Immaculate reservations about that material).<br /> <br /> \u200bI propose that you couldn't readily make a Beloved Adorai in the Second Age; that there's something in the tools, the knowledge, and the ingredients that is missing such that one generally can't make a 3-dot daiklave of that capability and power. Possibly also because of differences in the culture and the personalities; the Age of Sorrows still has larger-than-life people, but maybe not quite as large as the Solar that Adorei was made for (or even the one who made it). You still make something that is recognisably 3 dots, because that comes through mostly in the form and arrangement of the Evocations, but maybe not quite as powerful.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn contrast, I would look at something like Spring Razor, an Artifact of the same level made in the time of the Realm. I would describe that as being a bit more simple; its legend more straightforward, its Evocations a bit less nuanced. It has personality, but its personality is more direct; elegance, and poisoning people. Not exactly inferior as a weapon, but less elaborate.<br /> <br /> \u200bThen there's something like Sozen, with something around how its power is built around having created a false demon identity to slip into. I find that to be an example of an Artifact that is not only powerful, but legitimately mysterious; it, or the manner in which it was made, entailing a power that is not readily apparent to me. I can work with that to imagine ancient Artifacts whose workings entail knowledge that is lost, at least to the extent of somebody looking at it and having no idea of the process by which it was managed. For example, maybe it was based on some kind of foundation of sorcery, or social influence, things that a crafter in the Time of Tumult might be familiar with and even capable of, just not able to readily see underlying this suit of armour based on assuming the persona of a devil.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhile it's not strictly a subject of power, I do find this to be a perspective that does have an interaction with the 5-dot Artifacts, if only because I think we've only got two examples of those that weren't made in the First Age (one of which was a warstrider, benefiting both from being a thing of moving parts and described as cobbled together from scraps, the other being both from the very early Shogunate and with the aid of a Sidereal). The difficulty of making such powerful Artifacts is one that is built right into the system, but I do wonder if the characterisation could go a bit further; that these are ones that actually <i>do</i> require some kind of mystery behind them. The two in the core might be a bit borderline; arguably, things such as powering an Artifact with a hundred souls, or a dedicated volcanic manse is merely resource intensive, rather than dependent on lost occult knowledge, so something like them might be able to function as the Spring Razor to other 5 dots' Beloved Adorei. But when you've got things as uncanny as the Forgotten Blade, Gorgon and Stormcaller, I can see somebody looking at the thing and not only thinking it would be difficult, but hardly knowing where to begin.<br /> <br /> \u200bI've had ideas like this before, even if the system didn't really provide a hook to express them. I know they're not for everybody, with some people being repelled by the idea that the game could present something with a declaration that it's cooler than their character could make. They might not even be the intention of the writers. In any case, it's good for them not to be set in stone, so it shouldn't push people away.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut it's there enough for me to see it and take ideas from it, and I'm glad enough for that. It fulfils a notion I've spun for some time to my satisfaction.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd to be clear, it's not the kind of thing where I would even say making a new example of it is impossible; just that it might demand a bit more from the preamble, that the legend of your making something that could have powers like Sozen might entail solving the mystery of Sozen. After all, the powers of a new Artifact are already up in the air, and supposed to depend a bit on the story of how it was made, and not just fulfilling the mechanical requirements and laying down an outline of desired Evocations.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T08:58:29-08:00","id":1163019,"title":"","content":"So, Alchemicals using Artifacts.<br /> <br /> \u200bI can't say what the intention for the future is, but I personally don't see them being partially composed of the magical materials as necessarily a basis for having a special resonance with them. That's not me saying that it specifically means they shouldn't, just that I would see no contradiction if they didn't. It's presented as a primarily spiritual bond, so the material in common doesn't really make it definitive for me. I would find a stronger argument in the idea of the spiritual elements of an Alchemical arising from the material that they're made from being the basis of forming that bond, although even then not entirely, as I find the Alchemical Castes slightly distinct from the usual magical material associations or affiliated Exalted, especially regarding the Jade and Soulsteel Castes.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf one was to go with an idea that Alchemicals don't have special facility with Artifacts, I could even see ways of using being composed of magical materials as a basis for that; maybe some idea that being composed like that makes them similar enough to Artifacts themselves that actual Artifacts don't quite respond to them.<br /> <br /> \u200bMind, resonance and dissonance could also be incorporated some way into their Charms, in which case it wouldn't so much be a case of being bad with Artifacts as it would be expressing it in a different manner.<br /> <br /> \u200bPlus, I have a fondness of the implications that the Artifact of a Champion is on loan from the state, and if it came to a choice between that and rightful possession of the thing enough to develop Evocations, I would choose the former.<br /> <br /> I'll note that phrasing it all in terms of Alchemicals &quot;sucking&quot; at Evocations is overstating it a tad; even Dissonance doesn't constitute being bad with Evocations, just a limit on being able to get the most out of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T09:09:44-08:00","id":1163022,"title":"","content":"Alchemicals are designed to integrate Artifacts into their bodies. These are Alchemical Charms.<br /> <br /> They may not be so good at working with Artifacts which are NOT part of their bodies. This would not be a contradiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T09:16:07-08:00","id":1163023,"title":"","content":"I dunno, dissonance is a pretty big handicap in a lot of circumstances. If nothing else it provides a negative incentive for certain exalt types that makes taking artifacts made out of natively resonant stuff easier/better cost benefit ratio.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, my ST and I took a shot at homebrewing Alchemicals for our current game. They weren't meant to be PCs so we never did playtest them, but the way we handled resonances was we gave each caste a resonance with their own MM and are neutral to other MM. We went the route of Alchemicals having higher affinity with the MM but at a price: You could buy and install charms that upgraded your resonance with other MM. <br /> <br /> If you wanted to give incentives for having Alchemical characters utilizing artifacts made out of the same stuff they are, you could leave it at the level of resonating with your native material and either neutral or dissonant with the others, or if you wanted to really reduce their aptitude with artifacts and downplay any bonds with artifacts you could go neutral with caste material and dissonant with other MM.<br /> <br /> Either way, I think that Alchemicals alone it makes sense that it's a caste-specific resonance/dissonance scenario rather than something where the entire splat is resonant/neutral/dissonant with all of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T09:37:58-08:00","id":1163032,"title":"","content":"Maybe alchemicals could go in a different direction for their powerful effects. They only get neutral affinity with their caste material and dissonance with everything else, but Autochthonian artifacts have their most powerful effects gated behind physically interfacing with the alchemical's body or charms, and these &quot;jack in&quot; powers would be independent of resonance, meaning they were available to all alchemicals equally. Or maybe in some cases they would amplify resonance to encourage material matching or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T10:05:26-08:00","id":1163040,"title":"","content":"We've seen alchemical charms integrating artifacts into their bodies before. Interfacing and powering them up could definitely be one step further. <br /> <br /> Oh I also just remembered that there's another way to create the interchangeable artifacts scenario: Charm that has a pool of xp that can be committed to any attuned artifacts to unlock evocations. Probably only applicable to evocations that can be purchased with xp in the first place and less efficient than actually just buying them with xp, but could allow you to go from artifact to artifact. Downside to this is it severely reduces the metaphysical nature of the bond between exalt and artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T10:44:02-08:00","id":1163059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163023#post1163023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, dissonance is a pretty big handicap in a lot of circumstances. If nothing else it provides a negative incentive for certain exalt types that makes taking artifacts made out of natively resonant stuff easier/better cost benefit ratio.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Alchemicals are the only Exalted in Autochthonia, that hardly matters to them.<br /> <br /> In any case, I wasn\u2019t arguing that Alchemicals be dissonant with all Artifacts, or even universally neutral.<br /> <br /> I was only arguing that they would still make sense even if they weren\u2019t Resonant with any Artifacts. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the way we handled resonances was we gave each caste a resonance with their own MM and are neutral to other MM. </div> </div> </div>One wonders how much Jade counts as five different types as opposed to one. Maybe a Jade Caste is more strongly comprised of one form of jade than others?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We went the route of Alchemicals having higher affinity with the MM but at a price: You could buy and install charms that upgraded your resonance with other MM. </div> </div> </div>The new form of Material Synthesis Wave Emitter. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Either way, I think that Alchemicals alone it makes sense that it's a caste-specific resonance/dissonance scenario rather than something where the entire splat is resonant/neutral/dissonant with all of them. </div> </div> </div>I agree that it wouldn\u2019t make sense with anyone else since it wasn\u2019t done with the Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T10:50:06-08:00","id":1163060,"title":"","content":"I'd make it so that Alchemicals are dissonant and resonant with materials based on what charms they have at any time, for sure","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T10:53:11-08:00","id":1163061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163059#post1163059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Alchemicals are the only Exalted in Autochthonia, that hardly matters to them.<br /> <br /> In any case, I wasn\u2019t arguing that Alchemicals be dissonant with all Artifacts, or even universally neutral.<br /> <br /> I was only arguing that they would still make sense even if they weren\u2019t Resonant with any Artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>My comment was actually directly at Isator Levi's comments on how dissonance isn't 'being bad with evocations'. You posted while I was composing my reply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T10:58:54-08:00","id":1163063,"title":"","content":"If any exalt should be a master of artifacts to equal Solars I feel it would be Alchemicals. At the very least I would have them Resonant with the material matching their caste and have charms that give them resonance with the other materials.<br /> <br /> Alchemicals does bring up an interesting point. I'm really surprised that Adamant wasn't added as one of the core Magic Materials in 3e, even come up in discussion In Arms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T11:20:06-08:00","id":1163066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163063#post1163063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If any exalt should be a master of artifacts to equal Solars I feel it would be Alchemicals. At the very least I would have them Resonant with the material matching their caste and have charms that give them resonance with the other materials.<br /> <br /> Alchemicals does bring up an interesting point. I'm really surprised that Adamant wasn't added as one of the core Magic Materials in 3e, even come up in discussion In Arms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually specifically asked if adamant was considered a Magical material in Autochthonia in 3E and while the Devs did confirm that adamant caste was still a thing, they dodged the question on whether it was a MM in Autochthonia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T11:40:34-08:00","id":1163078,"title":"","content":"Adamant caste are secret. So it might be that it is a MM but nobody knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T20:19:09-08:00","id":1163151,"title":"","content":"One thing they made pretty clear in Arms is that the Five Magical Materials is a social classification, not a fundamental law of nature. Basically, the original Exalted Host found that, by using these four materials, they could produce artifacts that granted increased power to one or more of the types of Exalted. Thus, they named them the Magical Materials, and, as they were fairly plentiful, used them in practically everything.<br /> <br /> Adding Adamant to that classification wouldn't make much sense unless Exigents were universally resonant to it or something similar. Honestly, I think the only reason Soulsteel made it on the list is that ghosts have been using it for thousands of years and it was useful for Necromancy, which made it prominent enough before Abyssals showed up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T21:02:51-08:00","id":1163159,"title":"","content":"So, my opinions on moonsilver stuff.<br /> <br /> The expanded explanation of moonsilver's potentials is pretty cool. In particular, I like the details on what kinds of sorcery it could improve, especially as it means I was right about moonsilver being good for transmuting physical things into other physical things.<br /> <br /> Galliard is okay. It doesn't really grab me, but it makes perfect sense as half of a pair of &quot;sword-brother&quot; swords. I'm also a fan of character-fusion supermodes... it's just, I'm not so much interested in achieving it through swords.<br /> <br /> The Distaff is... weird. Sort of halfhearted. It doesn't really capitalize on &quot;web-weaving&quot; because its shape doesn't really make sense for it, like a pair of silk-weaving gloves might. The silk stuff is just a diversion from eventually hatching a completely different kind of sword, which isn't written up because it could be anything. The silk poppets are also a really weird jump from &quot;weave silk for things silk is useful for&quot; to &quot;weave autonomous servants out of silk&quot;. Seems like there's some excluded ground on simple things you could make from silk, like instantaneous nets or ropes or bridges or walls or trampolines.<br /> <br /> Frost-Thorn Knuckles are... Well, it's good at what it does, and what it does isn't pretty. That said, if you told me they were blue jade, I wouldn't have doubted you. This seems a little too literal a manifestation of minor lunar associations with cold. Very elemental. If we had any printed Lunar Charms, and this had any Evocations to upgrade such, this might have been salvaged as a &quot;moonsilver&quot; weapon in my eyes. I know it's more &quot;hunting/predation&quot; focused than blue jade normally would be, but I still can't believe no blue jade is at least included.<br /> <br /> The Tusk of Gallaech-Ma is cool. Very <i>Monster Hunter.</i> Very much the sort of thing I was looking forward to Lunar Exalted being able to craft for themselves.<br /> <br /> Flying Silver Dream is back, and better than ever. A very practical weapon for a Lunar who wants to benefit from an Artifact weapon while making full use of combat animal forms.<br /> <br /> Nightmare Shard is a useful assassin's weapon, capable of infecting others with madness with ambush attacks, retreating to let the sickness incubate, and then spying on the target to see how vulnerable they have become, then repeating the process until you're ready to murder them. Given this sort of cruelty, and the unpleasant experience of studying the weapon, it's no wonder its masters hate it.<br /> <br /> Unison is neat. Glad to get a sample of shapeshifting, merge-with-the-user armor. Also, it's practically right out of the <i>Crysis </i>games.<br /> <br /> I think the Walking Devil Tower is perfect for being the only moonsilver Warstrider in the book, and also a great use of moonsilver for making a Warstrider. It's also gratifying that its one of the only two Royal Warstriders in the book, and I like how its origin story merits that kind of honor. The Walking Devil Tower and Karvara are very cool and impressive.<br /> <br /> Overall very happy with the number and variety of moonsilver Artifacts in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-28-2017, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T21:28:07-08:00","id":1163162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163151#post1163151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing they made pretty clear in Arms is that the Five Magical Materials is a social classification, not a fundamental law of nature. Basically, the original Exalted Host found that, by using these four materials, they could produce artifacts that granted increased power to one or more of the types of Exalted. Thus, they named them the Magical Materials, and, as they were fairly plentiful, used them in practically everything.<br /> <br /> Adding Adamant to that classification wouldn't make much sense unless Exigents were universally resonant to it or something similar. Honestly, I think the only reason Soulsteel made it on the list is that ghosts have been using it for thousands of years and it was useful for Necromancy, which made it prominent enough before Abyssals showed up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making Magical Materials a culturalism is interesting. It would be neat to see how Autochthonia holds or doesn't hold that tidbit. Is it the five magical materials to them? Or is it the Six Greatest Gifts? Or something else entirely?<br /> <br /> Who knows!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T23:15:04-08:00","id":1163177,"title":"","content":"As one of the resident Alchemical fans, I'm going to say something odd. I think that Alchemicals might be universally Dissonant with artifacts and I think I'd be ok with it.<br /> <br /> To explain. Creation is a world where when you forge something, it has a soul. It is viewed as not just a sword, but as a unique product of craft, a one of a kind item. Something you can bond to and develop a relationship with. The Evocation system grows out of that.<br /> <br /> In Autochthonia, everything the mass produced, interchangeable, and issued to you by the government. Getting a set of personal tools you don't have to share is a nice perk, but if you break them, no big, you'll be issued another set, because individuals aren't important. Alchemical charms don't have souls, they're machines made to interface with and channel the power of an a Alchemical's soul. <br /> <br /> Artifacts coming from that culture would be fundamentally different and possibly be worth bringing back the term Magitech, since I think they'd probably be pretty similar to what came out of WotLA. Magical machines designed to do some extra cool things up front, but with underdeveloped souls that can't release extra powers later. Basically more like Interchangeable Charms that you could swap between two Alchemicals, instead of what Creation born think of as Artifacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 11-28-2017, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T23:39:32-08:00","id":1163178,"title":"","content":"The problem with &quot;Magitech&quot; as a word is it implies it's something distinct from normal magic or normal tech. And I don't think that's the case in Autochthonia. Even mortal industrial tech is often supported by Municipal Charms. Magic and technology are completely the same thing in Autochthonia, so there wouldn't be a distinct term for its mingling. At least not until people from Creation perhaps coined one to describe it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T23:44:32-08:00","id":1163180,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, I'd be cool with 1 dot Artifacts being introduced as a distinctly Autochthonian phenomenon, produced by the union of Municipal Craft Charms and mortal labor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T03:42:34-08:00","id":1163194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163159#post1163159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">its shape doesn't really make sense for it, like a pair of silk-weaving gloves might.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know; if one imagines it as an oversized version of an actual distaff (in a similar manner to ideas before about a rapier that could act as an acupuncture needle).<br /> <br /> \u200bTrue, distaffs are about spinning thread rather than weaving it, but still.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like there's some excluded ground on simple things you could make from silk, like instantaneous nets or ropes or bridges or walls or trampolines.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'd say those kinds of things are already covered under the stated capacity to craft items from silk. If one wishes more specialized Evocations for them, I don't think it would be too hard to custom develop them. Words devoted to giving the Distaff more Evocations are words that need to be taken away elsewhere.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T06:34:38-08:00","id":1163209,"title":"","content":"Yeah, things like nets are just going to be regular crafting projects.<br /> <br /> I kind of see what you mean about the shape though. I was looking at pictures of distaffs, but since there's no pedals or whatever, I'm not quite sure how to imagine a PC actually making stuff from it.<br /> <br /> It's a great artefact though. I like seeing these weird and wacky weapons that do things outside combat. One of the most interesting ones, conceptually, in the book.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T06:48:12-08:00","id":1163216,"title":"","content":"I mean a net that doesn\u2019t exist until you reflexively make one right before throwing it at someone. Like Spider-Man and his webshooters.<br /> <br /> In fact, based on Distaff, I want to see Evcoations for the Bracers is Universal Crafting. Or a version of those that produces silk. Because I love how Distaff\u2019s Evocations work with medicine and crafting, even if its shape just doesn\u2019t work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-28-2017, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T07:06:51-08:00","id":1163220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163078#post1163078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adamant caste are secret. So it might be that it is a MM but nobody knows.</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't really hold water considering that the Solars definitely used Adamant in a lot of artifacts. The Royal Warstrider Ascendant Nova Phoenix has a spherical fuselage made of the stuff. <br /> <br /> For some reason it's useful for crafting artifacts but it just isn't in the same class as the other MM... Not sure why they went this direction considering that makes alchemicals weird but... *shrug*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T07:12:25-08:00","id":1163221,"title":"","content":"I mean, if it's something simple like a bandage or cloth, I presume that you can just reach a spindle or your hand into the tangled thread, and pull a length of fabric out. For other things, I would presume that you actually require tools as surely as you do for any other crafting project, barring the use of Charms. Crafting and medicine actions both point out that they just assume such things are present and used for people applying those Abilities as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> \u200bA full loom is probably not often convenient, but a shuttle or needles might do the trick, particularly if a minor stunt is applied.<br /> <br /> \u200bAfter all, how does the shape of gloves fit more to the idea than a length of metal wrapped in thread? People don't weave and sew cloth with their bare hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T07:23:58-08:00","id":1163222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163220#post1163220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some reason it's useful for crafting artifacts but it just isn't in the same class as the other MM...</div> </div> </div> </div>In-character, soulsteel only really seems to be considered the same class as the other magical materials because it's associated with the Abyssal Exalted.<br /> <br /> \u200bI know it says that the magical materials are defined by their particular affinity for enchantment and capacity to bring out Evocations (which are still primarily a matter of the Exalted), but that connection seems to be what makes them; they each resonate with one of them, and the Solars have a stronger alignment with orichalcum even though they can resonate with everything.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt would be a bit out of place to have adamant in there with no particular affinity for any of the existing Exalted but still in the same class as your orichalcum and moonsilver rather than Malfean iron or behemoth ivory. Especially if only to foreshadow the Alchemical Exalted.<br /> <br /> \u200bOne could consider adamant to be regarded by the Autochthonians as a magical material on the same level as the other five because the Maker's brain is made out of it. After all, that's where the actual Adamant Caste Exalted tend to be made; within the Pole of Crystal, often within cities that are themselves elder Adamant Castes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T07:28:19-08:00","id":1163223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163220#post1163220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This doesn't really hold water considering that the Solars definitely used Adamant in a lot of artifacts. The Royal Warstrider Ascendant Nova Phoenix has a spherical fuselage made of the stuff.<br /> <br /> For some reason it's useful for crafting artifacts but it just isn't in the same class as the other MM... Not sure why they went this direction considering that makes alchemicals weird but... *shrug*</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty simple. it's in the &quot;other weird crap that nobody but solars can resonate with&quot; box. The bigger question is why soulsteel <i>isn't</i>, but that might be because of ghosts using it or maybe because as a metal it's easier to work with. That may have also been why Orichalcum got in, but the Dragon Kings' affinity for it could be another reason there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T07:53:15-08:00","id":1163229,"title":"","content":"Could be that while it\u2019s useful to other Exalted for getting specific effects out of Artifacts made primarily from other materials, actually getting full power evocations out of Adamant Artifacts is a secret possessed by Autochthon and passed by the Divine Ministers to their Operatives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T07:55:47-08:00","id":1163230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163223#post1163223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's pretty simple. it's in the &quot;other weird crap that nobody but solars can resonate with&quot; box. The bigger question is why soulsteel <i>isn't</i>, but that might be because of ghosts using it or maybe because as a metal it's easier to work with. That may have also been why Orichalcum got in, but the Dragon Kings' affinity for it could be another reason there.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're assuming that materials get added to the magical material list due to resonance. I don't think that's true in this edition. As you say, if it were, then soulsteel wouldn't be in the list at all. Arms describes the magical materials thusly:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arms of the Chosen page 12</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While many occult substances offer a suitable framework for kindling an artifact\u2019s power, none suit such purposes better than the five magical materials.</div> </div> </div> </div>This suggests that you get on the list based on innate ability to channel essence and inherent affinities that suit artifact construction. Adamant apparently doesn't rate that level of synergy. One wonders what the artifacts of the adamant caste will be if alchemicals resonate with their own material but not others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 11-28-2017, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T08:13:28-08:00","id":1163234,"title":"","content":"I'd also point out that 2E also had the '5 Magical materials' and then added a bunch more equally magical materials that resonate with other types of characters. (gossamer, infernal relics/vitriol tainted stuff, adamant. There may be more that I'm not remembering).<br /> <br /> In 3E it sounds like infernals are getting orichalcum, but unless adamant caste just get resonance with everything to better hide in Autochthonian society, they've gotta have adamant. It's seemingly a puzzle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T08:20:27-08:00","id":1163235,"title":"","content":"Gossamer could still be a MM for the purposes of fair folk. It just isn't counted because it doesn't really exist and the only way to get gossamer stuff is by stealing already complete artifacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T08:32:54-08:00","id":1163238,"title":"","content":"Speaking of adamant, I still want to design Cloud\u2019s Ultima Weapon as an adamant grand daiklave whose blade is clearest and sharpest when you are at your strongest and most focused.<br /> <br /> The more injured, pained, sick, and confused you are, the duller and more \u201cclouded\u201d the blade becomes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T08:40:37-08:00","id":1163241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163235#post1163235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gossamer could still be a MM for the purposes of fair folk. It just isn't counted because it doesn't really exist and the only way to get gossamer stuff is by stealing already complete artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gossamer could be an 'occult substance' or perhaps an 'exotic material', but if it was one of the magical materials the Fae wouldn't resonate with it. The last paragraph of the 'Magical Materials and the Exalted' section in Arms calls out Fae as one of those that doesn't normally resonate with the magical materials.<br /> <br /> Time and time again, 3E describes the MM as the &quot;most mystically potent substances known to the craftsmen and savants of creation&quot; both in the core and in Arms. Adamant has magical properties but it just isn't as potent as the big 5. This might be a distinction similar to comparing solar level with celestial level or terrestrial level in past editions. Fortunately the gap between exalted splats has been significantly closed in this edition.<br /> <br /> IE, the five MM are the highest tier of magical substances, Adamant would be alongside things like gossamer and behemoth ivory somewhere in the middle, while things like Feathersteel or Chiaroscuro glass might define the lower end of occult substances.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that this is canon btw, just that it seems to be the direction they're going in this edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T08:42:59-08:00","id":1163247,"title":"","content":"Hmm, alignment with the Exalted might not have been the right focus... more like the most straightforward kinds of Essence; the heavens, the earth, and the Underworld. It not being coincidental that the greatest deities align with those planes, and their corresponding types of Exalted (the Dragon Blooded having their own advantage even if there are Exigents stronger than them) come from them.<br /> <br /> \u200bSoulsteel is described as having been scarcely used in the First Age, but might have been considered among the other four even without a naturally aligned Exalt because it expressed that Essence of the Underworld. The magical materials, they all represent something iconic.<br /> <br /> What does adamant represent, again?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163234#post1163234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In 3E it sounds like infernals are getting orichalcum</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think people are reading a bit much into that. In context, I think orichalcum is supposed to gain a patina when ancient malefic sorceries are passed through it because oxidising metals have sinister connotations, verdigris patina is cooler than rust, and the actual mythical orichalcum has associations with copper (the literal translation from the Greek is &quot;mountain copper&quot;), which forms a verdigris patina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T08:58:56-08:00","id":1163256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163247#post1163247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What does adamant represent, again?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sharpness?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T09:01:08-08:00","id":1163259,"title":"","content":"I created a thread to talk about the potentials of adamant. We could revive it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T09:59:10-08:00","id":1163273,"title":"","content":"I'm already beaming over the buff this implies Dragon Blooded have gotten over previous editions (both as a DB fanboy and a GM looking for challenging antagonists). Resonant evocations are really good and a Realm Scion with their family jade daiklaive will be getting them as readily as a Solar. Multiply this times a sworn brotherhood and mix it with a few mortal battlegroups and it gets really easy to see why anybody but a limit breaking dawn caste is gonna strongly consider running from the Wyld Hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T11:23:28-08:00","id":1163286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163247#post1163247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI think people are reading a bit much into that. In context, I think orichalcum is supposed to gain a patina when ancient malefic sorceries are passed through it because oxidising metals have sinister connotations, verdigris patina is cooler than rust, and the actual mythical orichalcum has associations with copper (the literal translation from the Greek is &quot;mountain copper&quot;), which forms a verdigris patina.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Exalted it's clearly a magical analog/improvement on gold though, which doesn't rust or tarnish. I suspect the connotations of unnatural green discoloration in response to lengthy exposure to Sorcery are intentional.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T11:37:47-08:00","id":1163295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold(III)_oxide\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/16/Au2O3structure.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold(III)_oxide\" target=\"_blank\"> Gold(III) oxide - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold(III)_oxide\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold(III)_oxide </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Takes some work, but gold can tarnish, aka oxidize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T11:40:35-08:00","id":1163296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163247#post1163247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What does adamant represent, again?</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally see it as kind of an anti-Moonsilver, associated with Order, Clarity, Stability, and Permanence. But it has some paradoxical overlap in that &quot;clarity&quot; can also be &quot;invisibility&quot; when its clear enough, and obviously bending/refracting light can be good justification for illusion evocations (see Crystal Chameleon Style Martial Arts, or the mind-fuckery of the Adamant Caste Anima power). One writer for 2E (I forget who) said they thought of it as having the same associations that unite the different colors of Jade if you took out the overt elemental powers - hence the Seal Piercing Municipal Charm being made from Jade and Adamant: Jade links links to Creation and Adamant to Autochthonia in the same way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T12:04:16-08:00","id":1163303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163296#post1163296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> One writer for 2E (I forget who) said they thought of it as having the same associations that unite the different colors of Jade if you took out the overt elemental powers</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll go ahead and say that while that was fine for Second Edition artifice, it's not a sound concept for a magical material on which Evocations can be based. In whatever book introduces pure adamant artifacts, it'll likely get a thematic write-up similar to those of other materials in Arms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T12:17:42-08:00","id":1163305,"title":"","content":"I do like the idea of Adamant being &quot;sharpness&quot;<br /> <br /> Like, it's one word. But so's &quot;fire&quot; and so's &quot;mutability&quot;<br /> <br /> Sharpness can mean a lot of things. Sharp stuff is clear, direct, it is clean and pure. Sharpness means clarity. Sharpness turns effort into result with maximum efficiency. Things that are sharp are often very hard, and very strong. Scalpels that cut to heal are sharp, swords that kill, minds that create, eyes that see, these things are all within the purview of Adamant. I am writing artifact for my next campaign at the moment and I feel like each magical material has a personality which can be transcribed into evocations of various types with a mechanical expression of that personality, and I feel that &quot;sharpness&quot; does that for Adamant very effectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T15:40:07-08:00","id":1163361,"title":"","content":"I just had the stupidest idea ever.<br /> <br /> The Twin Crescent Stone makes a temporary duplicate of any one-handed weapon. This duplicate functions <i>exactly</i> like the original, meaning it has all its evocations. This allows you to use evocations that would normally damage the weapon without having to repair it. For instance, you can use Adorei's <i>Blade Dance of the Warrior Wed</i> in every fight (surely there is no risk to duplicating the jealous Adorei), or can use Sekhem's <i>Stronger than Fire</i> without having to repair it afterwards. Now I just need a sword with a ridiculous and otherwise-cheap Broken Phantasm-style effect to completely break the game. Does this make the third way to pull off Unlimited Blade Works in Exalted, to one degree or another? Or the fourth?<br /> <br /> Sadly, the Distaff has no hearthstone sockets, so my plan of repeatedly using <i>Quicksilver Rebirth</i> on a duplicate to unveil a new daiklave whenever I please will have to go unfulfilled. Although... hmm, Gnomon has a hearthstone socket, so I could duplicate it, harvest a peach from the duplicate...<br /> <br /> There's other tricks with it, too. If you have three hearthstone sockets, you could combine Twin Crescent Stone + Root-of-the-Earth Gemstone + Gem of the Wind Blade to throw duplicates of your sword that weigh a ton. Unfortunately you'd sort of have to make puppy-dog eyes at your ST to houserule whether you can pin people at range with them. The Twin Crescent Stone is also vague on whether you can create a second duplicate while an earlier one still exists.<br /> <br /> Observation: The Jewel of the Rabbit's Sword does not have a rule forbidding you from using it on craft or sorcerous workings (a restriction quite wisely placed on eg. Arete.) If your ST doesn't hit you with a book when you try it, it can completely eliminate any risk of botching on long-term projects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 11-28-2017, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T16:48:47-08:00","id":1163386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163295#post1163295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold(III)_oxide\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold(III)_oxide</a><br /> <br /> Takes some work, but gold can tarnish, aka oxidize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting! How the hell did anyone ever find that out given the materials and circumstances involved?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T16:57:52-08:00","id":1163391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163386#post1163386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How the hell did anyone ever find that out given the materials and circumstances involved?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYou see, there are these people called scientists. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bMore serious version of that answer; I would presume it was a case of forming a hypothesis based on known properties of matter such as the valence of gold, how metals typically oxidise, and how things such as acids work, and then performing experiments in a lab to manipulate the substances following the logic of that hypothesis until they got information from which they could extract conclusions. With that information, you continuously refine the hypothesis (possibly until it evolves into a theory), and ultimately they achieved a result of being able to form a compound that probably couldn't exist in nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T17:08:06-08:00","id":1163399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163386#post1163386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting! How the hell did anyone ever find that out given the materials and circumstances involved?</div> </div> </div> </div>Isator Levi gave the long-short answer. The short short answer is Scientists are usually funded, passionate, and curious.<br /> <br /> Funding+Passion+Curiousity=Science","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T17:24:40-08:00","id":1163405,"title":"","content":"Aquillion, you are a mad genius, you!<br /> <br /> Let's see, all the different cool options...<br /> <br /> Courante&amp;Gailliard = duplicates of either and/or both of these are going to be <i>interesting </i>to figure out how the pairings work. Also, for the capstone, fusions fusing together with multiple pairs possible?<br /> <br /> Irenio's Bell = dual wielding shields is always fun, but also, logically, both shields get Vibration whenever you block attacks. Actually really, really strong combo, you could have so much Defense from spending the Vibrations. Also, capstone at E4, you could summon two 2nd Circle Demons at once, for maximum overkill.<br /> <br /> Rainwalker = With just 2 hearthstones, you could have FOUR SHIELDS (dual wielding Irenio's Bells, while having two Rainwalkers levitate by your side).<br /> <br /> Razor Dancer&amp;Wise Steel = similar paired sword shenanigans as Courante&amp;Gaillard, but only potentially, since having two Razor Dancers doesn't make the Form any different. <b>Perfect </b>Soulsteel duplicates, though... are the souls also duplicated?<br /> <br /> Sun's Brush = you would really need Exalted-like hand-eye coordination to write two things at the same time, for once! :P <br /> <br /> Tusk of Galaech-Ma (only when mounted) = two quarries at once, baby!<br /> <br /> Asphodel = okay, this one's just strange <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You can have two different hidden worlds with 2 different Shou Ren's? In any case, very good for &quot;Broken Phantasm&quot; shenanigans, you could empty the hidden world of the duplicate Asphodel and still have retainers on the real artifact.<br /> <br /> Flying Silver Dream = remember the 4 shields approach up there? Now add two flying swords to the mix for the ultimate blender. And if you somehow get incapacitated even with all that arsenal, the capstone is going to be terrifying for any enemies still left standing when the blades go berserk.<br /> <br /> Gnomon (can Wrackstaffs be used one-handed anyway?) = things can quickly get very JoJo's Bizarre Adventure when you can stop time <i>while stopping time. </i>Also, as Aquillion pointed out, more peaches.<br /> <br /> Mist-Weaver = that's a lot of fog, or you could combo a 100 mile radius normal fog with a smaller, location specific supernatural fog.<br /> <br /> Talion = similar to the Tusk, you can have two grievances at once.<br /> <br /> Forgotten Blade = what would happen if you would use the duplicate to try to erase the actual artifact from memory? Nothing, even the attuned would forget, or something crazier metaphysically?<br /> <br /> Gorgon = at least for the capstone, it would help against the &quot;narratively appropriate botch sets the demon free&quot; clause.<br /> <br /> Stormcaller = here's the truly crazy stuff, combine with Single Point and Steel Devil for ALL THE STORMS, ALL THE TIME! Well, the most effective way would be to use Single Point with one sword, who keeps constantly releasing Intensity 1 blasts, and using the other sword normally to gather more Intensity for a big killing blow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15678-cenrei","name":"Cenrei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15678_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T17:26:24-08:00","id":1163407,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, &quot;how the hell did anybody figure that out given the materials and circumstances involved&quot; is a fairly good way to approach the difficulty of recreating the ancient mysteries of how somebody might have created something like Beloved Adorei or Sozen, the Cataphract of Keys that I was talking about before. Like I said, you need to already know quite a bit about the underlying structure and properties of various materials before you can even do something like hypothesize how they might interact under extraordinary and/or artificial circumstances. That's the kind of thing that took quite a while to figure out from scratch (not least because the investigation existed in circumstances that weren't quite amenable to dedicated scientific research, even if they were rarely really actively hostile to them; progress is slow when one of your only real sources of scientific inquiry is bored and curious rich people). So a major loss of something like scientific literacy would conceivably take a while to recreate a lot of that knowledge so that things like research can be resumed and certain technologies can be applied again.<br /> <br /> Think about the chain of information that would be needed to get everything required for the kinds of experimentation that let you find a stable oxide of gold, and then imagining it all being destroyed, and you could have an answer to the question of why it might take so long to rediscover secrets that the First Age took for granted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T17:37:53-08:00","id":1163410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163407#post1163407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, &amp;quot;how the hell did anybody figure that out given the materials and circumstances involved&amp;quot; is a fairly good way to approach the difficulty of recreating the ancient mysteries of how somebody might have created something like Beloved Adorei or Sozen, the Cataphract of Keys that I was talking about before. Like I said, you need to already know quite a bit about the underlying structure and properties of various materials before you can even do something like hypothesize how they might interact under extraordinary and/or artificial circumstances. That's the kind of thing that took quite a while to figure out from scratch (not least because the investigation existed in circumstances that weren't quite amenable to dedicated scientific research, even if they were rarely really actively hostile to them; progress is slow when one of your only real sources of scientific inquiry is bored and curious rich people). So a major loss of something like scientific literacy would conceivably take a while to recreate a lot of that knowledge so that things like research can be resumed and certain technologies can be applied again.<br /> <br /> Think about the chain of information that would be needed to get everything required for the kinds of experimentation that let you find a stable oxide of gold, and then imagining it all being destroyed, and you could have an answer to the question of why it might take so long to rediscover secrets that the First Age took for granted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't like this enough. My attitude on DotFA isn't that magitech emulates modern day tech. Its that it emulated modern day society and culture and not the methods that led to them. Motonic physics is dumb. The first age being the result of massive information infrastructures that lead to impossible wonders.<br /> <br /> Key is wonders. Blessed Ardorei is the result of the mystic understanding of sword and soul. Not an AI.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T17:42:42-08:00","id":1163411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163361#post1163361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just had the stupidest idea ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stupid? Or <i>clever?</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Twin Crescent Stone is also vague on whether you can create a second duplicate while an earlier one still exists. </div> </div> </div>No, that's clearly not right.<br /> <br /> You shouldn't be able to make another duplicate unless someone tries to grab the first. Or maybe you pop the Hearthstone out and back in. Or maybe you can just will the lost duplicate to disappear, which makes more sense.<br /> <br /> But having two duplicates is too many.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T18:07:02-08:00","id":1163419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163411#post1163411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that's clearly not right.<br /> <br /> You shouldn't be able to make another duplicate unless someone tries to grab the first. Or maybe you pop the Hearthstone out and back in. Or maybe you can just will the lost duplicate to disappear, which makes more sense.<br /> <br /> But having two duplicates is too many.</div> </div> </div> </div>As written, the only thing that makes the duplicate disappear is if it's wielded by another. So if I throw it at you (after making it weigh a ton with Root-of-the-Earth Gemstone and using Gem of the Wind Blade to make it throwable, if necessary), I still have the original in my hand and can use its ability to create another duplicate as a misc action - nothing in the description of how making duplicates work cares if another duplicate already exists somewhere.<br /> <br /> And as written, the first duplicate doesn't disappear until / unless someone else tries to wield it.<br /> <br /> (As written, it doesn't disappear <i>ever</i> until someone else tries to wield it or wields the original.)<br /> <br /> Also, it occurs to me that I could theoretically throw the original, then use the duplicate to create more duplicates, since it's a perfect copy. There's no practical reason why I'd want to do this (if anyone grabs the original, all duplicates disappear, whereas each duplicate only disappears individually if it's wielded by someone else), but you can do it.<br /> <br /> What I really want is a sentient sword with the power to take its own actions and activate its own hearthstones' abilities. Then I could duplicate it exponentially and, using Root of the Earth Gemstone, bury the entire world under ridiculously heavy copies.<br /> <br /> ...but since the weapon needed to do that doesn't really exist, most of the exploits for this aren't <i>that</i> bad. And chain-duplicating weapons so you can throw them doesn't really cause any problems, especially given that it's a miscellaneous action every time you want to pull out a new one. Even with the Very Heavy Copy trick, as written you can only pin people who are already prone (and you technically have to make puppy-dog eyes for your ST to let you do it at range even with the Gem of the Wind Blade, although most would probably allow it since it makes logical sense and doesn't break anything.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 11-28-2017, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T18:10:57-08:00","id":1163421,"title":"","content":"Aquillion, anyone at my table (had I a table), who tried those sorts of shenanigans would get smacked by the corebook. (Not literally, the core book is heavy. Maybe by Miracles though.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T18:18:02-08:00","id":1163423,"title":"","content":"Also, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Nw_cdqQHGA8\" target=\"_blank\">my thoughts on reading Hawk's Star Jess</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163421#post1163421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aquillion, anyone at my table (had I a table), who tried those sorts of shenanigans would get smacked by the corebook. (Not literally, the core book is heavy. Maybe by Miracles though.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the Twin Crescent + Wind Blade trick isn't even particularly powerful, just amusing. There's no reason not to allow it - a dedicated artifact throwing weapon would be better anyway and would come back. Even throwing in a Root-of-the-Earth Gemstone is only as powerful as the ST allows it to be, since there aren't actually any rules for throwing your really heavy sword (and the most logical ruling is &quot;ok, you can use it to pin prone people at a distance using the gambit&quot;, which is fun but hardly game-breaking.)<br /> <br /> The Broken Phantasm / Unlimited Blade Works trick is substantially more powerful, but it depends heavily on what weapon they use it with. I wouldn't allow it with Adorei, but as I implied, there's in-setting reasons why doing so could backfire in weird ways, since I doubt Adorei would appreciate having a duplicate.<br /> <br /> I think it's also logical to rule that duplicates vanish when you're no longer wielding them (possibly allowing them to exist long enough to perform a thrown attack with them, since that doesn't really break anything). Or that they vanish when you make a new duplicate, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 11-28-2017, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T18:19:20-08:00","id":1163424,"title":"","content":"Twin Crescent Stone is so vaguely written to be awesomely broken in potential. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> One thing that could actually limit it is, do you have to attune to the duplicates independently? So, you COULD have a million floating Flying Silver Dreams, but you couldn't attune to all of the duplicates?<br /> <br /> Also, you technically don't even need to have the original with you to create the duplicates. &quot;While this moonstone is socketed in an attuned one-handed artifact weapon, the Exalt can create a duplicate of the weapon from moonlight and shadow as a miscellaneous action.&quot; You could have your original at home, but attuned to you and just go on using duplicates. (Heh, evil Storytellers can use this trick to stop the players from looting all that sweet sweet artifact loot from defeated enemies)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15678-cenrei","name":"Cenrei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15678_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T19:00:08-08:00","id":1163432,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, it never says the duplicate appears next to you. It may appear next to the artifact.<br /> <br /> Also attunement lapses if you go a day without touching the artifact in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T19:12:31-08:00","id":1163435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163432#post1163432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, it never says the duplicate appears next to you. It may appear next to the artifact.<br /> <br /> Also attunement lapses if you go a day without touching the artifact in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be such a wonderful way to thwart any player who tried that trick! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> &quot;Ok, now that everything is in place, I will start to build up my arsenal for tomorrow! I use my miscellaneous action to make a duplicate of my artifact! And then repeat that forever!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Ok, you do that. Back home, under your sealed vault where you left your artifact, a duplicate appears right next to the original&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;-_-&quot;<br /> <br /> But that second part, about attunement lapsing after a day, gives me a storyhook...<br /> <br /> Entire Creation could be filled to the brim with endless, unattuned copies of the Forgotten Blade. Swords everywhere, but you forget about them the minute it leaves your sight. Also, you remember it if you look at it, but if you touch it, it disappears (since it is a duplicate). How do you know that RIGHT NOW, behind every corner there could be a Forgotten Blade duplicate, dangerously poking out of the wall?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15678-cenrei","name":"Cenrei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15678_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T19:32:44-08:00","id":1163440,"title":"","content":"Devs, if you're reading this thread, maybe see if you can add in a couple more &quot;vanish&quot; conditions for the Twin Crescent duplicates?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T19:36:55-08:00","id":1163442,"title":"","content":"I really don't think that's necessary. Jokes aside it's pretty obvious how the hearthstone is supposed to work and any &quot;endless duplicate&quot; shenanigans should rightly be responded to by swatting players with a rolled up newspaper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T21:28:17-08:00","id":1163472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163440#post1163440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Devs, if you're reading this thread, maybe see if you can add in a couple more &quot;vanish&quot; conditions for the Twin Crescent duplicates?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately, someone's already posted this in the errata thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T09:44:34-08:00","id":1163585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163423#post1163423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Broken Phantasm / Unlimited Blade Works trick is substantially more powerful, but it depends heavily on what weapon they use it with. I wouldn't allow it with Adorei, but as I implied, there's in-setting reasons why doing so could backfire in weird ways, since I doubt Adorei would appreciate having a duplicate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think a &quot;HE'S MINE!&quot; &quot;NO, MINE!&quot; struggle would be the inevitable result of that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T06:58:41-08:00","id":1163897,"title":"","content":"So, what mecha do you guys most want to see translated into Exalted as Warstriders?<br /> <br /> We\u2019ve got the essence of most punchy Japanese \u201cSuper Robots\u201d with All-Conquering Colossus, who evokes Gypsy Danger. Also GaoGaiGar with its Heaven (Blue) and Hell (Red) fists. <br /> <br /> We\u2019ve got the essence of most American-style \u201cBattletech and Imperium of Man Warhammer\u201d mecha with Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation. Also the Terran Thor of Starcraft 2.<br /> <br /> We\u2019ve got something like Wing Gundam with Ascendant Nova Phoenix, and probably the best possible translation of Evangelions with Walking Devil Tower. <br /> <br /> What else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-30-2017, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T07:33:19-08:00","id":1163906,"title":"","content":"Gurren Lagann. Let's have warstriders so big you have to pilot them from inside a regular-sized warstrider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T07:37:40-08:00","id":1163911,"title":"","content":"I'm currently working on rules for an alteration of warstrider stats for use in a cramped environment such as Autochthonia. I figure they'd be built mech warrior style with no heads, short squat bodies and shorter limbs. Doing my best to balance it so that a creation strider would be at a disadvantage in Autochthonia and the reverse would be true as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T07:40:24-08:00","id":1163913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163906#post1163906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gurren Lagann. Let's have warstriders so big you have to pilot them from inside a regular-sized warstrider.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lagann\u2019s example reminds me of a concept for another moonsilver Warstrider I want to see. <br /> <br /> One designed entirely to fuse and combine with another Warstrider to make it stronger.<br /> <br /> Like the Lagann, or the White Falcon Zord which wasn\u2019t necessary to complete the Ninja Megazord, but which could attach to it to give it the power of flight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T07:53:29-08:00","id":1163919,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know if a Dev has mentioned the area of the Storm effect for Stormcaller?<br /> <br /> Not the sheath effect, the initial storm.<br /> <br /> Also, single point says it's custom to sheath every strike, but it's not mandatory. So I guess there wouldn't be any real issue using these two very cool things together?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T08:26:10-08:00","id":1163930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163897#post1163897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what mecha do you guys most want to see translated into Exalted as Warstriders?<br /> <br /> We\u2019ve got the essence of most punchy Japanese \u201cSuper Robots\u201d with All-Conquering Colossus, who evokes Gypsy Danger. Also GaoGaiGar with its Heaven (Blue) and Hell (Red) fists. <br /> <br /> We\u2019ve got the essence of most American-style \u201cBattletech and Imperium of Man Warhammer\u201d mecha with Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation. Also the Terran Thor of Starcraft 2.<br /> <br /> We\u2019ve got something like Wing Gundam with Ascendant Nova Phoenix, and probably the best possible translation of Evangelions with Walking Devil Tower. <br /> <br /> What else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Liberty Prime is soemtging a player of mine desperately wants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T08:46:47-08:00","id":1163939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163919#post1163919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know if a Dev has mentioned the area of the Storm effect for Stormcaller?<br /> <br /> Not the sheath effect, the initial storm.<br /> <br /> Also, single point says it's custom to sheath every strike, but it's not mandatory. So I guess there wouldn't be any real issue using these two very cool things together?</div> </div> </div> </div>Should reach Extreme:<br /> &quot;Within seconds,<br /> the sky grows dark, the wind picks up, and rain begins to<br /> fall out to four range bands from Stormcaller.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> And on single point... it works. You don't lose much if anything iirc from not sheathing the sword.<br /> It does follow the fluff that sheathing it is kind of an exercise in restraint, lest you might murder too much. Goes well with Stormcaller in that sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 11-30-2017, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T09:11:52-08:00","id":1163949,"title":"","content":"Durrr, thanks! Should read more carefully haha.<br /> <br /> Yeah I'm making a Demon Hunter character and I wanted to draw on Single Point and Stormcaller as they're thematically appropriate. And Violet Bier, which doesn't exist, but I'd like to homebrew up a charm tree (and I've found some other homebrews too so should be able to nail it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T09:49:08-08:00","id":1163962,"title":"","content":"I think there\u2019s maybe one Single Point Charm that explicitly requires sheathing, but it is one of the ancillary Charms later in the style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T10:32:50-08:00","id":1163975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163897#post1163897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what mecha do you guys most want to see translated into Exalted as Warstriders?<br /> <br /> We\u2019ve got the essence of most punchy Japanese \u201cSuper Robots\u201d with All-Conquering Colossus, who evokes Gypsy Danger. Also GaoGaiGar with its Heaven (Blue) and Hell (Red) fists. <br /> <br /> We\u2019ve got the essence of most American-style \u201cBattletech and Imperium of Man Warhammer\u201d mecha with Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation. Also the Terran Thor of Starcraft 2.<br /> <br /> We\u2019ve got something like Wing Gundam with Ascendant Nova Phoenix, and probably the best possible translation of Evangelions with Walking Devil Tower. <br /> <br /> What else?</div> </div> </div> </div>You already mention a Jaegar, but i\u2019d love a particularly giant Warstriders that requires two pilots who become mentally linked in co-attunement. They each get to invest to separate Evocations that they get to wield all of in combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T10:36:23-08:00","id":1163976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163911#post1163911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">warstrider stats for use in a cramped environment such as Autochthonia.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not using this to comment on your own plans specifically, so much as the overall attitude as it comes up:<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's... not exactly odd that people tend to refer to Colossus Alchemicals and possible warstriders in Autochthonia as untenable, but it does represent a point of forgetting or disregarding the point that there are supposed to be fairly large open spaces there as well. Not just the kinds of chambers that nations and towns are situated in, but much more sizable ducts and tunnels and the occasional fairly deep pit or high domed space throughout the Reaches. They're not ubiquitous, but they are frequent enough for larger beings to have room to operate in, and the premise of Autochthonia is such that it does not stretch plausibility for these points to be sufficiently accessible and interconnected that a Colossus or behemoth could get to work.<br /> <br /> \u200bSure, the more human sized spaces create environments in which those subjects can't act, but it's not as if the regular warstrider doesn't have those as well, such as upon boats (or just about anything to do with the water for a warstrider that is not made to be aquatic, or the inside of any structure that you don't intend to smash apart.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T11:11:20-08:00","id":1163989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163975#post1163975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You already mention a Jaegar, but i\u2019d love a particularly giant Warstriders that requires two pilots who become mentally linked in co-attunement. They each get to invest to separate Evocations that they get to wield all of in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, hey, maybe you would be interested in this thread I made a while back to discuss how a Warstrider with multiple pilots could work!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1102579-two-heads-are-better-than-one-warstriders-and-monsters\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1102579-two-heads-are-better-than-one-warstriders-and-monsters\"> Two Heads Are Better Than One (warstriders and monsters) - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1102579-two-heads-are-better-than-one-warstriders-and-monsters\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1102579-two-heads-are-better-than-one-warstriders-and-monsters </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> What if a Warstrider had a cockpit for two pilots at once? Like a Pacific Rim Jaeger. Each character piloting the warstrider rolls Join Battle and tracks her own </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It also includes an idea for Alchemical Colossi having a cockpit Charm that would let an Alchemical Champion plug into them to serve as a \u201csecond pilot\u201d, with similar benefits!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T13:49:30-08:00","id":1164045,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not joking when I say that I want a Warstrider which is also a tree.<br /> <br /> Someone used magic and sorcery to cultivate a tree into the shape of a Warstrider, and they made a Wood-aspected manse-tree to provide the Treestrider with its Hearthstone.<br /> <br /> The Treestrider has some unique maintenance requirements that, when met, allow it to regenerate damage on its own.<br /> <br /> If it\u2019s ever fully destroyed, the manse-tree starts growing a massive nut or fruit in which you can find a replacement Treestrider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T13:57:58-08:00","id":1164050,"title":"","content":"I actually really like that. Would it have magical materials mixed in, or purely be a magic tree?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T14:50:11-08:00","id":1164069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1164050#post1164050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually really like that. Would it have magical materials mixed in, or purely be a magic tree?</div> </div> </div> </div>I want green jade, but am not entirely sure how to factor it in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T14:59:14-08:00","id":1164075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1164069#post1164069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want green jade, but am not entirely sure how to factor it in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Grow the tree around the green jade, like the burning spear we have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jea