-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T15:25:07-08:00","id":1164084,"title":"","content":"I think that's appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T15:29:40-08:00","id":1164086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1164077#post1164077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The burning branch didn\u2019t grow from jade, though?<br /> <br /> Also, I kind of like the idea that the Treestrider uses raw green jade stone, without any metal at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe more like this is what I meant?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/gIXULiS.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/gIXULiS.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/gIXULiS.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://i.imgur.com/gIXULiS.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T17:47:48-08:00","id":1164110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1164075#post1164075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grow the tree around the green jade, like the burning spear we have.</div> </div> </div> </div>You carve the cockpit from a giant piece of green jade and let the tree grow around it, using green jade bands on the branches and green jade carved stones on the ground to shape the essence flowing in to the tree. I think that should do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T21:34:55-08:00","id":1164173,"title":"","content":"Take a sapling. Bury a bunch of pure green jade around it. Water it every day with water infused with ground jade and alchemical growth solution. Sing hymns to Sextes Jylis and the wood elementals to it every day. When it grows to be a biiiiiiiiiiiiiiiig, strong tree, use specially blessed orichalcum, moonsilver, and adamant chisels and begin carving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/740-anaximander","name":"Anaximander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T23:10:42-08:00","id":1164185,"title":"","content":"I feel like you'd want to use a seed from one of the skyscraper sized redwoods in the uttermoast east for this. Part of the whole manse, green jade, alchemical fertilizer, etc. would be to get that kind of growth in a few years instead of centuries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T02:46:49-08:00","id":1164211,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if the image I had of a warstrider made from trees grown into that shape was something that came out of your description or if it was just my own imagination going in its own direction, but if it was me I'd look for something that would preserve that.<br /> <br /> \u200bI've had thoughts in the past about jade deposits being leeched up into things like trees, which would take the form of a tree with veins of jade running along the trunk or even something more fantastical like living flesh with jade leaves and flowers, but right now something feels missing from that.<br /> <br /> I'd wonder at the idea of creating a framework of jade that binds and bends the trees as they grow, with a long term purpose of getting them to weave together, but wonder if that might not be a bit too mundane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T03:41:15-08:00","id":1164216,"title":"","content":"This Treestrider talk got me thinking about potential other Warstriders. Like, maybe a Warstrider that is only a Black Jade cockpit, but when it is submerged, it forms a body out of water (maybe by beckoning water elementals, since that's also one of Black Jade's purviews)?<br /> <br /> Or a Soulsteel &quot;skeleton&quot; with a cockpit made out of a dead behemoth's heart, blood vessels connecting the heart to the skeleton. When the Warstrider is activated, the Soulsteel forms phantasmal flesh and muscle out of the souls trapped inside the Soulsteel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15678-cenrei","name":"Cenrei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15678_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T03:45:30-08:00","id":1164217,"title":"","content":"If we're going this route, why bother with a cockpit? Maybe the whole thing is just talismans or a suit of normal armor that conjures a phantasmal giant body made of energy around the wearer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T04:01:22-08:00","id":1164218,"title":"","content":"I feel as though you've got an issue when you have something that heavily belies the usual mass and cost of a warstrider, and any implications of that.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, sure, in mechanical terms the difference between one made of thousands of pounds of magical material and something a lot smaller is ultimately the same in the craft system, but it can affect the verisimilitude of it. It certainly has much bigger implications for the matter of transporting them.<br /> <br /> If the point is to figure out a way to integrate warstriders into stories where they wouldn't usually be feasible, that's fine, but as an overall thing I'd say they have about the same issues as being able to conjure them with sorcery does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T04:03:59-08:00","id":1164219,"title":"","content":"A warstrider that portable that can fit in tight spaces that one shouldn't normally fit or that can be deactivated and reactivated easily mid-battle to deal with a single enemy would provide utility that would probably push it to N/A level. It's straight up better than the big clunky versions.<br /> <br /> That said, I am totally down for an N/A armour/warstrider being a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 12-01-2017, 07:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T05:18:24-08:00","id":1164229,"title":"","content":"I admit I was being a little facicious, but it's not actually a bad idea","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T06:39:09-08:00","id":1164246,"title":"","content":"I've actually got a few ideas how it might work. Basically the Warstrider mode would be an evocation that cost maybe 10-15 motes and could only be activated while there was a greater hearthstone in one of the armour's slots.<br /> <br /> Damage would manifest on the armour somehow, and have to be repaired for the usual cost and difficulties. I was thinking maybe a cape that gradually gets torn or crystals that get cracked. Possibly both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T07:24:55-08:00","id":1164256,"title":"","content":"Any one else think of the Ents from LoTR with this talk of tree-warstriders?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T07:35:27-08:00","id":1164261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1163976#post1163976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not using this to comment on your own plans specifically, so much as the overall attitude as it comes up:<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's... not exactly odd that people tend to refer to Colossus Alchemicals and possible warstriders in Autochthonia as untenable, but it does represent a point of forgetting or disregarding the point that there are supposed to be fairly large open spaces there as well. Not just the kinds of chambers that nations and towns are situated in, but much more sizable ducts and tunnels and the occasional fairly deep pit or high domed space throughout the Reaches. They're not ubiquitous, but they are frequent enough for larger beings to have room to operate in, and the premise of Autochthonia is such that it does not stretch plausibility for these points to be sufficiently accessible and interconnected that a Colossus or behemoth could get to work.<br /> <br /> \u200bSure, the more human sized spaces create environments in which those subjects can't act, but it's not as if the regular warstrider doesn't have those as well, such as upon boats (or just about anything to do with the water for a warstrider that is not made to be aquatic, or the inside of any structure that you don't intend to smash apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly why I think that warstriders have a home in the Autochthonian setting. However given that there a lot more places where you could get stuck in one and headroom could become an issue, I tweaked the rules such that any area that had less than 2 ranges bands horizontally and/or one range band vertically, regular warstriders would be at a disadvantage. Especially with heavy or medium melee weapons. Damn hard to swing a 20 ft sword when your head is scraping the ceiling after all. I basically assume that Autochthonian striders (and colossi) make the most of the room that's available. However, I also didn't want to make Autochthonian strider to be completely superior to their creation counterparts. Since I'm integrating the head into the torso to give extra room up top it makes sense that visual acuity would suffer.<br /> <br /> As to the warstrider I'm currently working on it actually takes it a step further. It's evocations are centered around warping space and it essentially shrinks itself down to human sized to better go through tunnels. It's actually still full sized, it just buggers with local space. <br /> <br /> As for Colossi, I figure that being an actual creature of that size wouldn't impose the same penalties to action in cramped spaces. Hence Colossi would be similar to creation's warstriders in form but wouldn't suffer the same penalties in Autochthonia. Thus giving them an edge in big open spaces fights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T14:31:14-08:00","id":1164390,"title":"","content":"Now that I've actually had more time to read more of Arms of the Chosen, I'm glad to finally have it. I haven't read everything yet, but from what I've seen, there are a lot of interesting artfacts in here that I'd like to use in a game. And I've always tended to play characters that don't rely on equipment, so that's saying a lot.<br /> <br /> Warstriders are pretty great, too. At a glance they seem terrifyingly powerful, but not always and entirely better than artifacts of the same rating (which are also terrifyingly powerful), depending on the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/157-phoenix_kensai","name":"Phoenix_Kensai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar157_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T16:31:48-08:00","id":1164421,"title":"","content":"My main issue with Arms, and artifacts in general, is this. My character is using the Charm &quot;Immaculate Golden Bow&quot;.<br /> <br /> With this Charm, he has an artifact bow made out of his own soul and experiences, which makes that particular weapon most suited to him, and he has grown fond of it. Even if he were to come across another artifact bow, I don't think he would give up on using his own bow, no matter how cool the artifact would be. <br /> <br /> Well, I guess my main gripe might actually be that those spontaneous artifact creation Charms are narratively too good to stop using... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15678-cenrei","name":"Cenrei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15678_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T16:47:54-08:00","id":1164426,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15678-cenrei\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar15678_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"15678\" data-vbnamecard=\"15678\">Cenrei</a> iirc the devs said that charms such as that and saber can have evocations, they may not be at the level of artifact 5, but they can infact be on par with a 3 dot artifact. Though this does require homebrewing the evocations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T23:09:09-08:00","id":1164473,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I have worked with my GM to create Evocations for my bow, symbolic of the journey my character took that resulted in his Exaltation. That's part of why I said they're narratively too powerful, they fit the character much better than any artifact they could find, since those Evocations come from the soul and experiences of the character. Only thing comparable would be a Craft character creating an artifact for themselves, a crafter also wouldn't replace his creation with a weapon he just found.<br /> <br /> One way to establish similar narrative connection with published artifacts would be just to say that the artifact was your character's previous incarnation's weapon. But I feel that has become a cliche used too much in Exalted, so I don't like that method. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15678-cenrei","name":"Cenrei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15678_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T03:11:28-08:00","id":1164493,"title":"","content":"Certainly there's nothing wrong with a character who is most concerned with their own Immaculate Golden weapon, but there's a whole range of effects that probably aren't available through that, whether due to the material or the general legend of the Artifact.<br /> <br /> If none of the Artifacts in the book grabbed you then that's fine, but I don't think it can be denied that the book provided a wide range of compelling and useful Artifacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T04:34:55-08:00","id":1164504,"title":"","content":"Evocations that are symbolic of your character are fine, but one of the big draws of artifacts is that they allow you to expand your capabilities. IGB or GSS evocations are a pure expression of self, but the evocations you get out of a red jade daiklave are a <i>communal</i> expression of you, the sword, the sword's previous wielders and its creator. <br /> <br /> No man is an island, y'know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T07:02:14-08:00","id":1164520,"title":"","content":"Plus, I'm sure there's room for merging an Immaculate Golden Bow with an artifact bow to use their Evocations together. At least sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T07:22:38-08:00","id":1164525,"title":"","content":"Plus if you're not super invested in archery or melee you can get by with an artifact and get your evocations with solar exp while you save the regular sort for the stuff closer to your niche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T09:08:21-08:00","id":1164549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1164045#post1164045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not joking when I say that I want a Warstrider which is also a tree.<br /> <br /> Someone used magic and sorcery to cultivate a tree into the shape of a Warstrider, and they made a Wood-aspected manse-tree to provide the Treestrider with its Hearthstone.<br /> <br /> The Treestrider has some unique maintenance requirements that, when met, allow it to regenerate damage on its own.<br /> <br /> If it\u2019s ever fully destroyed, the manse-tree starts growing a massive nut or fruit in which you can find a replacement Treestrider.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://agtp.romhack.net/project.php?id=jutei\" target=\"_blank\">Jutei Senki</a> has that, although it doesn't really have a plot or characters so there's not much in-depth focus on it outside of the art design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T09:15:03-08:00","id":1164550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1164504#post1164504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Evocations that are symbolic of your character are fine, but one of the big draws of artifacts is that they allow you to expand your capabilities. IGB or GSS evocations are a pure expression of self, but the evocations you get out of a red jade daiklave are a <i>communal</i> expression of you, the sword, the sword's previous wielders and its creator.<br /> <br /> No man is an island, y'know?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure IGB or GSS evocations necessarily have to be an expression of self. The sword itself starts as one, but it's not necessarily your <i>entire</i> self, so to speak; it can represent a specific aspect of yourself, with specific memories and themes contributing to it. This specificity allows you to (and to an extent requires you to) branch out with it rather than having its evocations just be Solar charms you can buy with Solar XP.<br /> <br /> So if you're someone who cares a lot about your family and lineage, your GSS might express that and might have evocations related to it. If you really really hate injustice, your GSS might grow in that direction. In that respect it can be like any other artifact, just one whose initial theme has significant personal meaning to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T09:57:42-08:00","id":1164558,"title":"","content":"Don't forget how Immaculate Golden weapons can also be an embodiment of one's anima; if your iconic manifestation is an eagle or a lion, there's no reason that the Evocations can't be more about something symbolised by those than it is about the character's personality.<br /> <br /> I mean, sure, one of the things that your iconic banner symbolises is your personality, I'm just saying it doesn't need to be limited to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T09:25:30-08:00","id":1165592,"title":"","content":"I've finally read through the book and simply wanted to say that I really loved the weapons, found the armors kind of hit and miss (style, not rules) and really liked the warstriders. The Hearthstones are a lot better than the core ones, but still mostly not worth their point cost to me. The general artifacts also are certainly an improvement.<br /> Overall I'm very happy with the book, though I do wonder how the artifacts will hold up once more exalts have been released.<br /> Has anything been said about how that'll be handled?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2UIUH9oaJnHMWIxcVdGMjNUYlE\" target=\"_blank\">3EX Martial Arts basic overview (Weapons, Armor, Attributes &amp; Abilities)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","name":"Edward Eldritch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T19:03:03-08:00","id":1166221,"title":"","content":"The various splat books should have their own sections of Artifacts with native Evocations and such things in them. Other than that, not really. That said, I imagine that if/when they do another Artifact book, that book will have more widely spread native evocations in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T22:09:03-08:00","id":1166244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1166221#post1166221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The various splat books should have their own sections of Artifacts with native Evocations and such things in them. Other than that, not really. That said, I imagine that if/when they do another Artifact book, that book will have more widely spread native evocations in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arms also gives a lot of leeway on things like customizing and the devs have ven more or less said it's pretty easy for things that require Solar Charms to just swa-in the other Exalt equivilant. I imagine often things an Evocation that requires All-Encompassing Sorcerer's sight might require Pulse of the Invisible for a Lunar or Telltale Symphony for a Sidereal.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T07:30:28-08:00","id":1166275,"title":"","content":"That said, it would seem easier for Solars to find ways to enhance orichalcum Evocations with their native Charms, which is all the incentive they need to favor orichalcum even when they're equally Resonant with all Artifacts.<br /> <br /> Compatibility goes beyond mere Resonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T12:30:17-08:00","id":1166514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1166275#post1166275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, it would seem easier for Solars to find ways to enhance orichalcum Evocations with their native Charms, which is all the incentive they need to favor orichalcum even when they're equally Resonant with all Artifacts.<br /> <br /> Compatibility goes beyond mere Resonance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine with solars being the sole masters of orichalcum, by dint of being masters of all evocations.<br /> There's no need to scale orichalcum up for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T14:25:05-08:00","id":1166533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1166514#post1166514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no need to scale orichalcum up for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that how you see it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T16:21:46-08:00","id":1166560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cenrei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1164473#post1164473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I have worked with my GM to create Evocations for my bow, symbolic of the journey my character took that resulted in his Exaltation. That's part of why I said they're narratively too powerful, they fit the character much better than any artifact they could find, since those Evocations come from the soul and experiences of the character. Only thing comparable would be a Craft character creating an artifact for themselves, a crafter also wouldn't replace his creation with a weapon he just found.<br /> <br /> One way to establish similar narrative connection with published artifacts would be just to say that the artifact was your character's previous incarnation's weapon. But I feel that has become a cliche used too much in Exalted, so I don't like that method. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The solution I intend to use: if a character has GSS or IGB <i>as well as</i> an Artifact weapon, and would like to address the redundancy, I would permit as a Storyteller,or ask for as a player, that the two become one over time, and the Artifact is now the weapon within the character's soul. Mechanically, you treat it like Summoning the Loyal Steel, but I see a few more effects.<br /> <br /> 1) One free Evocation from the new Artifact. You spent XP on a Charm to address your lack of an Artifact, but now you have one. An Evocation is roughly equivalent.<br /> 2) Either let the existing Evocations from the Charm weapon carry over, or trade them for the new weapon's Evocations with training time, player's choice preferably. One per downtime, though - can't take a year off and go from capstone to capstone. That would be boring. Got to grow into the new powers.<br /> 3) Sweet Evocations with GSS or IGB as a prereq.<br /> 4) I see this as a deeper bond than usual, so let the weapon's nature start altering the character's anima in a way reflective of the weapon as more Evocations are bought. I do this anyway, but I would accelerate it a little in this instance.<br /> <br /> Same principles would work for GSP and armor.<br /> <br /> Just my ideas, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T19:55:57-08:00","id":1166586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Edward Eldritch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1165592#post1165592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall I'm very happy with the book, though I do wonder how the artifacts will hold up once more exalts have been released.<br /> Has anything been said about how that'll be handled?</div> </div> </div> </div>The artifacts in Arms clearly all have the &quot;this is what a Solar might get if wielding the weapon&quot; charm trees - this is most noticeable with <i>Strife's Crucible</i>, an artifact that was made by a particular Sidereal and which has never been wielded by anyone else, yet has an evocation that does nothing but upgrade <i>Majestic Radiant Presence</i>, a Solar charm. (Although, noticeably, that evocation is just sort of branching off the main tree and isn't a prerequisite to anything else, so it's pretty easy to take it out, move it around, or replace it with an upgrade to whatever other charm you decide is relevant if you want.)<br /> <br /> The book specifically says that some evocations are deliberately gated off by Solar charms to block access for power-level reasons (this is most obvious with Stormcaller, which has HTT as a prerequisite right before going into an evocation that directly replicates one of the most iconic Solar Circle Sorcery spells), but it's also clear that some of them are meant to have substituted versions for other Exalts with similar charms (eg. the Arms evocation tree for Unison, an artifact made by a Lunar and obviously designed with Lunars in mind, specifically seems to upgrade all the Solar charms that Lunars are likely to have parallels to.)<br /> <br /> Of course, another possibility is that Exalts will share some charms - that is, Lunars might have Increasing Strength Exercise itself or whatever. There have always been a few charms like that, but evocations make it actually meaningful, since you could eg. give all Exalts that are supposed to have access to a particular thematic one specific charm, then use it as a prerequisite in evocation trees so it works for all of them with no tinkering. Or some charms could specifically say that they can be used as another charm for the purpose of Evocation prerequisites, although if it's not <i>exactly</i> identical this could cause problems with upgrade evocations, which seem to be very common.<br /> <br /> I suspect that each splat's own book will have a lot of artifacts that work with that splat's charms, but that artifacts elsewhere will generally reference Solar ones for two reasons:<br /> <br /> 1. Everyone has the corebook, but also,<br /> <br /> 2. Solar charms tend to be simple and are most &quot;generic&quot;, which means they're the ones shared between the most other Exalts, thematically (and also, going by previous editions, literally.) It's usually a lot easier to substitute a Lunar charm for a Solar charm than it is to substitute a Lunar charm for a Sidereal charm, say.<br /> <br /> (Also, noticeable that the charms used as prerequisites in Arms tend to be the most generic and straightforward Solar ones - the ones that other Exalted are likely to have versions of, and the ones it's easiest to identify parallels for. You see lots of upgrades for eg. HTT, no upgrades for God King's Shrike. Granted, those simple ones tend to be base charms many people will have - an artifact that upgrades the persona charms would be a bit wasted on most people, though it'd clearly be a cool thing to have.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 12-12-2017, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T20:21:48-08:00","id":1166590,"title":"","content":"I keep wondering how many people keep missing the KEY part on evocation design on page 19 <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><b>Charm Enhancements: </b>These Evocations upgrade one or more of the wielder\u2019s Charms in a way that fits the themes of the artifact. Note that any Evocations that require, e.g., a Solar Charm Enhancement will only be accessible to Solars, which can be used to gate off effects that would be disruptively overpowered in the hands of weaker wielders.</span> </div> </div> </div>And then don't apply it to literally all the Evocation Lines in the book. Literally all of them are designed to be used as templates for home brewing up artifacts, with the added benefit of being off the shelf ready for solar players*. I would literally not take any of the artifacts in question as gospel for each splat but as Aquillion says, to provide interchange ability between splats.<br /> <br /> *I am being semi-hyperbolic for dramatic effect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T09:19:05-07:00","id":1207298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1162364#post1162364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is definitely not the interest of Exalted 3e by default to have minion warstriders.<br /> <br /> If you want to put them in, I\u2019d just make them without evocations. It\u2019s... kind of bland, but hey, if you want minion striders, that\u2019s kind of the result of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could not some warstrider version of Distaff's &quot;silk puppets&quot; evocation solve that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T18:45:32-07:00","id":1208660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen#post1158815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know who the character is on the front cover? Is she new or am I just forgeting things?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201c<i>Silence is not empty or immaterial, and it is not needed to chain tame things. It often guards powers strong enough to shatter everything.</i>\u201d <div align=\"right\">- Emmi It\u00e4ranta, Memory of Water</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> That would be the Chosen of Silence, Exigent resident at my heart - if I may be allowed to be some 5 months and 24 pages late.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm looking at the cover. Hearing the quote that inspired the character. And thinking there could be no better fit than this.<br /> Arms of the Chosen (of Silence)..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":81,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/81-vx3","user":"VX3","date":". 04-18-2018, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/81-vx3","name":"VX3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar81_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T08:46:40-07:00","id":1208896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VX3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1208660#post1208660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u201c<i>Silence is not empty or immaterial, and it is not needed to chain tame things. It often guards powers strong enough to shatter everything.</i>\u201d <div align=\"right\">- Emmi It\u00e4ranta, Memory of Water</div><br /> <br /> <br /> That would be the Chosen of Silence, Exigent resident at my heart - if I may be allowed to be some 5 months and 24 pages late.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm looking at the cover. Hearing the quote that inspired the character. And thinking there could be no better fit than this.<br /> Arms of the Chosen (of Silence)..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Huh, I had no idea. Where'd you get that from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T09:24:06-07:00","id":1208910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VX3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1208660#post1208660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u201c<i>Silence is not empty or immaterial, and it is not needed to chain tame things. It often guards powers strong enough to shatter everything.</i>\u201d <div align=\"right\">- Emmi It\u00e4ranta, Memory of Water</div><br /> <br /> <br /> That would be the Chosen of Silence, Exigent resident at my heart - if I may be allowed to be some 5 months and 24 pages late.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm looking at the cover. Hearing the quote that inspired the character. And thinking there could be no better fit than this.<br /> Arms of the Chosen (of Silence)..</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you're happy with it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T08:43:17-07:00","id":1211823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1208910#post1208910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad you're happy with it!</div> </div> </div> </div>Very happy! In all the abundance of details I provided with the character, I couldn't have asked for a better context in which to depict her.<br /> <br /> The Chosen of Silence attends to those who seek silence, and those who remained in silence for far too long. So it was only a matter of time before she made her way into AoC's cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/81-vx3","name":"VX3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar81_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}